1
00:00:00,931 --> 00:00:03,934
♪ In the not too
distant future ♪

2
00:00:03,934 --> 00:00:07,110
♪ Somewhere in time and space

3
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:10,182
♪ Mike Nelson and
 his robot pals ♪

4
00:00:10,182 --> 00:00:13,496
♪ Are caught in
 an endless chase ♪

5
00:00:13,496 --> 00:00:16,533
♪ Pursued by a woman
 whose name is Pearl ♪

6
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:19,571
♪ An evil gal who wants
to rule the world ♪

7
00:00:19,571 --> 00:00:22,608
♪ She threw a few
 things in her purse ♪

8
00:00:22,608 --> 00:00:24,472
♪ And in a rocket
 ship she hunts him ♪

9
00:00:24,472 --> 00:00:26,509
♪ All across the universe

10
00:00:26,509 --> 00:00:29,063
- [Pearl] I'll get you!

11
00:00:29,063 --> 00:00:32,135
♪ I'll send him cheesy movies

12
00:00:32,135 --> 00:00:34,586
♪ The worst I can find

13
00:00:34,586 --> 00:00:35,932
♪ La-la-la

14
00:00:35,932 --> 00:00:38,383
♪ He'll have to sit
 and watch them all ♪

15
00:00:38,383 --> 00:00:40,661
♪ And I'll monitor his mind

16
00:00:40,661 --> 00:00:42,007
♪ La-la-la

17
00:00:42,007 --> 00:00:44,596
♪ Now keep in mind,
 Mike can't control ♪

18
00:00:44,596 --> 00:00:47,047
♪ Where the movies
 begin or end ♪

19
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:48,048
♪ La-la-la

20
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:50,429
♪ He'll try to keep his sanity

21
00:00:50,429 --> 00:00:55,400
♪ With the help of
 his robot friends ♪

22
00:00:56,194 --> 00:00:57,402
♪ Robot roll call

23
00:00:57,402 --> 00:00:58,886
♪ Cambot 
 - You're on.

24
00:00:58,886 --> 00:01:00,232
♪ Gypsy 
 - Oh my stars.

25
00:01:00,232 --> 00:01:01,647
♪ Tom Servo 
- Check me out.

26
00:01:01,647 --> 00:01:03,304
♪ Crow 
- I'm different.

27
00:01:03,304 --> 00:01:06,342
♪ If you're wondering how
 he eats and breathes ♪

28
00:01:06,342 --> 00:01:08,723
♪ And other science facts

29
00:01:08,723 --> 00:01:10,173
♪ La-la-la

30
00:01:10,173 --> 00:01:12,451
♪ Just repeat to yourself,
 it's just a show ♪

31
00:01:12,451 --> 00:01:15,420
♪ I should really just relax

32
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:19,700
♪ For Mystery Science
 Theater 3000 ♪

33
00:01:22,944 --> 00:01:26,707
[doors whirring and closing]

34
00:01:33,507 --> 00:01:35,647
- Help! [chuckles]

35
00:01:35,647 --> 00:01:37,166
Help!

36
00:01:37,166 --> 00:01:38,408
- Crow, what is it?

37
00:01:38,408 --> 00:01:39,892
- Hey Mike, give me a
 hand here, will you?

38
00:01:39,892 --> 00:01:42,481
I'm having a real problem
 with my Thighmaster.

39
00:01:42,481 --> 00:01:44,000
Probably should've
looked at the directions

40
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,554
before I started
messing with it, but no,

41
00:01:46,554 --> 00:01:49,385
I just had to work
 on my trouble spots.

42
00:01:49,385 --> 00:01:51,628
- Hey Crow, did you know
this was a Thaw Master?

43
00:01:51,628 --> 00:01:52,526
- What?

44
00:01:52,526 --> 00:01:54,114
A Thaw Master?

45
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:56,737
Well, how do you
 like that? [chuckles]

46
00:01:56,737 --> 00:01:58,187
- Hi Mike, hi Crow.

47
00:01:58,187 --> 00:02:00,120
Say guys, breakfast is
gonna be a little late.

48
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,845
This pot roast just
 won't thaw yet.

49
00:02:01,845 --> 00:02:03,537
There's something wrong
with the Thaw Master.

50
00:02:03,537 --> 00:02:06,195
No Servo, this is a Thighmaster.

51
00:02:06,195 --> 00:02:07,057
- A Thighmaster?

52
00:02:07,057 --> 00:02:07,989
Well, no wonder.

53
00:02:07,989 --> 00:02:09,198
[all laughing]

54
00:02:09,198 --> 00:02:10,544
- This is never gonna thaw.

55
00:02:10,544 --> 00:02:11,821
We'll be right back.

56
00:02:11,821 --> 00:02:12,649
- Son of a gun.

57
00:02:12,649 --> 00:02:13,547
That's good.

58
00:02:13,547 --> 00:02:16,136
[upbeat music]

59
00:02:20,899 --> 00:02:21,831
Thaw Master, Thighmaster.

60
00:02:21,831 --> 00:02:24,385
Thighmaster, Thaw Master.

61
00:02:24,385 --> 00:02:26,042
Reminds me of that
 time I tried to wear

62
00:02:26,042 --> 00:02:27,975
that hand-hammered
 wok for underpants.

63
00:02:27,975 --> 00:02:29,079
- Yeah, that really...

64
00:02:29,079 --> 00:02:30,598
Hey, Mrs. Forrester's calling.

65
00:02:31,772 --> 00:02:33,705
- We'll begin with
 a frontal cut.

66
00:02:33,705 --> 00:02:34,947
- But has he been washed?

67
00:02:34,947 --> 00:02:36,777
- I washed him
 earlier with my mind.

68
00:02:36,777 --> 00:02:37,916
It was not pleasant.

69
00:02:37,916 --> 00:02:38,986
Hi guys.

70
00:02:38,986 --> 00:02:41,747
Things have
deteriorated down here.

71
00:02:41,747 --> 00:02:44,854
Unless I'm mistaken,
 and frankly, what
 are the odds of that?

72
00:02:44,854 --> 00:02:47,753
The brain guys are
 about to dissect Bobo.

73
00:02:47,753 --> 00:02:49,686
Say, could we get on
 with this dissection?

74
00:02:49,686 --> 00:02:51,792
I think it's almost mealtime.

75
00:02:51,792 --> 00:02:53,897
- Bobo's very stupid.

76
00:02:53,897 --> 00:02:56,452
Anyway, I'm locked in
 some kind of force-field.

77
00:02:56,452 --> 00:02:58,902
[electricity humming]

78
00:02:58,902 --> 00:03:00,904
So here's the deal.

79
00:03:00,904 --> 00:03:04,080
I know you guys despise
me, even loathe me.

80
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,702
So could you help me out?

81
00:03:05,702 --> 00:03:06,979
- Careful, careful.

82
00:03:06,979 --> 00:03:08,981
- I need a distraction
 of some kind.

83
00:03:08,981 --> 00:03:11,260
If you can think of
 something, I promise

84
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:14,608
to never show you
another bad movie again.

85
00:03:15,471 --> 00:03:16,610
Really.

86
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:17,921
Never again, ever.

87
00:03:17,921 --> 00:03:19,440
- Hmm, you think
 we can trust her?

88
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:21,235
- I don't know.

89
00:03:21,235 --> 00:03:23,099
- Pwease?

90
00:03:23,099 --> 00:03:25,274
Pwease, pwetty
 pwease, for Pearl?

91
00:03:26,896 --> 00:03:29,209
Pearl needs a
 distraction so bad.

92
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:30,244
Pwease?

93
00:03:30,244 --> 00:03:31,763
Come on.

94
00:03:31,763 --> 00:03:33,351
For Pearl.

95
00:03:33,351 --> 00:03:34,904
Pwease?

96
00:03:34,904 --> 00:03:36,733
- Ugh.
 - My god, stop it!

97
00:03:36,733 --> 00:03:37,700
- Okay, fine, fine.

98
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,184
Just don't do that.

99
00:03:39,184 --> 00:03:41,669
Maybe the nanites have an idea.

100
00:03:41,669 --> 00:03:44,879
Hello, nanites, could
 you create a distraction?

101
00:03:44,879 --> 00:03:46,087
- Distraction?

102
00:03:46,087 --> 00:03:47,537
Cool.
 - I know, I know, I know.

103
00:03:47,537 --> 00:03:49,608
We can send a fleet of tiny
ships down there to pants them.

104
00:03:49,608 --> 00:03:52,024
- Well, gee, that seems
kinda complicated.

105
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:52,853
- I know.

106
00:03:52,853 --> 00:03:54,164
Simpler, sure, okay.

107
00:03:54,164 --> 00:03:56,028
I know, we could always
biosynthesize an android

108
00:03:56,028 --> 00:03:59,100
and send down there to
 say, Hey, look over there.

109
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:01,033
- Great, why don't you
 just cut the tractor beam

110
00:04:01,033 --> 00:04:02,207
that's holding us here?

111
00:04:02,207 --> 00:04:04,036
- Ah, fine, a
 number three, sure.

112
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:05,762
- We never get to
 do anything fun.

113
00:04:05,762 --> 00:04:06,625
There, it's done.

114
00:04:07,937 --> 00:04:08,869
- Hey, great.

115
00:04:08,869 --> 00:04:09,801
How's that, Mrs. Forrester?

116
00:04:09,801 --> 00:04:11,389
Is that distracting?

117
00:04:11,389 --> 00:04:12,631
- What the devil was that?

118
00:04:12,631 --> 00:04:13,839
- Very distracting.

119
00:04:13,839 --> 00:04:14,771
- Yes.

120
00:04:14,771 --> 00:04:15,910
- Observer, you remain here.

121
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:17,843
And I will check it out.

122
00:04:17,843 --> 00:04:18,879
- Certainly.

123
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:19,845
- Guard.

124
00:04:19,845 --> 00:04:20,881
Hey, guard.

125
00:04:20,881 --> 00:04:22,848
I got a sick man in here.

126
00:04:22,848 --> 00:04:23,677
- Do you mean me?

127
00:04:23,677 --> 00:04:24,505
Because I'm not sick.

128
00:04:24,505 --> 00:04:25,472
I'm being dissected.

129
00:04:25,472 --> 00:04:26,714
- Shut up.
 - Okay.

130
00:04:26,714 --> 00:04:29,338
- Your friend Observer
created an invisible man

131
00:04:29,338 --> 00:04:31,512
with his mind and put
 him in here with me.

132
00:04:31,512 --> 00:04:33,273
- I suppose that's possible-

133
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:36,310
- Yeah, and now he's
 looking real sick.

134
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:38,036
Uh-oh, you better
 get in here quick.

135
00:04:38,036 --> 00:04:39,589
I don't think you'd
 want him to die.

136
00:04:39,589 --> 00:04:41,108
- Well, where is here?

137
00:04:41,108 --> 00:04:42,937
- Well, he's right
 over there, look.

138
00:04:42,937 --> 00:04:44,870
Oh boy, he sure looks bad.

139
00:04:44,870 --> 00:04:46,147
- I'm sorry, I'm just not-

140
00:04:46,147 --> 00:04:47,356
- kay, beautiful,
 you and your brain

141
00:04:47,356 --> 00:04:49,047
are coming with me, Mister.

142
00:04:49,047 --> 00:04:50,945
- Oh, don't hurt
 my brain, please.

143
00:04:50,945 --> 00:04:52,222
- Everything's nice
 and comfortable.

144
00:04:52,222 --> 00:04:54,294
Everybody's okay.

145
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:56,261
Just keep coming with me.

146
00:04:56,261 --> 00:04:58,332
Come on, Bobo, we're
getting off this planet.

147
00:04:58,332 --> 00:04:59,299
- Wouldn't it be
 more polite to wait

148
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:00,576
until after I'm dissected?

149
00:05:00,576 --> 00:05:01,577
- Shut up!
 - Okay.

150
00:05:01,577 --> 00:05:02,509
- You put down that thing!

151
00:05:02,509 --> 00:05:03,406
- I'm not putting down that!

152
00:05:03,406 --> 00:05:07,307
[all shouting at once]

153
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:08,756
Mike, I accidentally lied.

154
00:05:08,756 --> 00:05:10,689
Your movie today
is She Creature.

155
00:05:10,689 --> 00:05:12,001
I'm not putting down the thing!

156
00:05:12,001 --> 00:05:15,245
[all shouting at once]

157
00:05:16,281 --> 00:05:17,662
- She Creature?

158
00:05:17,662 --> 00:05:19,595
You know who I'm thinking
 is a she creature?

159
00:05:19,595 --> 00:05:20,458
Huh?
- Yeah?

160
00:05:20,458 --> 00:05:21,321
- Huh?
- Yeah?

161
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:22,563
- Huh?
 Yeah?

162
00:05:22,563 --> 00:05:24,082
- Hey, I tried to steer
us away from the planet,

163
00:05:24,082 --> 00:05:27,327
but the stupid smart guys have
 cut our navigational system.

164
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,190
- Well, maybe the
 nanites can take care

165
00:05:29,190 --> 00:05:30,606
of that little problem, huh?

166
00:05:30,606 --> 00:05:32,504
- Yeah, we'll fix your little
 problem for you, uh-huh.

167
00:05:32,504 --> 00:05:35,058
Hey Steve, Mr. Nelson wants
 a number seven, pronto.

168
00:05:35,058 --> 00:05:36,715
- Well there you go,
 that took care...

169
00:05:36,715 --> 00:05:38,061
Hey, what's a number
 seven, anyway?

170
00:05:38,061 --> 00:05:42,790
[explosion booming]
 [all shouting]

171
00:05:42,790 --> 00:05:44,620
- Mike, you blew
 up another planet!

172
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,138
What is your deal?

173
00:05:46,138 --> 00:05:48,244
- I just told 'em to take
 care of a little problem.

174
00:05:48,244 --> 00:05:49,418
- And they did!

175
00:05:49,418 --> 00:05:51,523
Here comes Mike,
 destroyer of worlds.

176
00:05:51,523 --> 00:05:54,733
- Oh god of fire and
 vengeance, stay away from me.

177
00:05:54,733 --> 00:05:55,941
Get away from me.

178
00:05:55,941 --> 00:05:58,116
[alarm buzzing]
 - We got movie sign.

179
00:05:58,116 --> 00:06:01,878
[doors whirring and opening]

180
00:06:10,577 --> 00:06:12,544
- Planet killer.
- I didn't, it's not me.

181
00:06:12,544 --> 00:06:15,823
- This is as colorful as
the movie's gonna get.

182
00:06:15,823 --> 00:06:17,791
- [Tom] Ah, The RuPaul Story.

183
00:06:17,791 --> 00:06:20,276
[eerie music]

184
00:06:21,726 --> 00:06:23,900
- [Mike] Hey, Tim Conway as
 Dorf is going to be in this.

185
00:06:25,557 --> 00:06:27,387
- [Tom] Hey, there's Tim Finn.

186
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:28,836
There's Gil Hodges.

187
00:06:28,836 --> 00:06:30,251
There's Gil Gerard.

188
00:06:30,251 --> 00:06:31,701
There goes Joe Pesci.

189
00:06:31,701 --> 00:06:33,185
There's Prunella Scales.

190
00:06:33,185 --> 00:06:35,360
There's Abe Vigoda.

191
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:37,397
Is there a sturgeon
 in the house?

192
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:39,019
Can I borrow a fin?

193
00:06:41,055 --> 00:06:45,094
- Sea turtle.
- Yes, I do. [laughing]

194
00:06:45,094 --> 00:06:48,477
Based on drunken comments
 made one night by Lou Rusoff.

195
00:06:48,477 --> 00:06:50,582
- At least the production
 was supervised.

196
00:06:50,582 --> 00:06:52,481
Things didn't get out of hand.

197
00:06:52,481 --> 00:06:55,449
- [Tom] Clearly the ocean
 does not have metered ramps.

198
00:06:55,449 --> 00:06:56,623
Oh, it's humid today.

199
00:06:56,623 --> 00:06:58,038
Oof.

200
00:06:58,038 --> 00:06:59,384
[thunder crashing]

201
00:06:59,384 --> 00:07:01,351
- Oh, Lee Trevino goes fishing.

202
00:07:03,181 --> 00:07:04,354
- [Mike] Samuel Z. Dunkoff.

203
00:07:04,354 --> 00:07:06,978
- [Tom] Yeah, Samuel
 Z. Wienerhead.

204
00:07:06,978 --> 00:07:08,462
- [Mike] Well, I think
 ideally it should be

205
00:07:08,462 --> 00:07:10,153
related to his name.
 - Oh.

206
00:07:11,327 --> 00:07:13,985
Hey, there's Bennett
 Cerf, and Billy Ocean!

207
00:07:13,985 --> 00:07:15,193
- [Mike] Stop it, Servo.

208
00:07:16,746 --> 00:07:19,818
- Once again folks, a
Golden State Production.

209
00:07:19,818 --> 00:07:21,302
- [Tom] Is this a
 Show-Me-State Production?

210
00:07:21,302 --> 00:07:23,615
- No, I think it's a
Golden State Production.

211
00:07:23,615 --> 00:07:24,547
- [Mike] Wait a minute,
wasn't it already

212
00:07:24,547 --> 00:07:25,755
produced by someone?

213
00:07:28,102 --> 00:07:29,587
- [Tom] Edward Cahn, Edward
 Cahn, let me rock it,

214
00:07:29,587 --> 00:07:31,071
that's all I wanna do.

215
00:07:31,071 --> 00:07:34,833
Edward Cahn, let me rock
 you, that's all I wanna do.

216
00:07:38,181 --> 00:07:39,389
- Gidget meets Magritte.

217
00:07:40,839 --> 00:07:43,532
- [Carlo] Now, on this
very night, I am calling

218
00:07:43,532 --> 00:07:45,395
from the unknown
 depths of time itself.

219
00:07:45,395 --> 00:07:46,396
- [Tom] Uh-huh, and you are?

220
00:07:46,396 --> 00:07:48,778
- [Carlo] And she is here.

221
00:07:48,778 --> 00:07:51,194
And with her coming, the
 world will never be as it was.

222
00:07:51,194 --> 00:07:52,782
- [Tom] Your Fluffer
 Nutters spilled.

223
00:07:52,782 --> 00:07:54,853
- [Narrator] Neither man
 nor animal will be the same.

224
00:07:54,853 --> 00:07:56,096
- Nor manimal.

225
00:07:56,096 --> 00:07:58,995
- [Carlo] This, I,
 Dr. Carlo Lombardi,

226
00:07:58,995 --> 00:08:00,549
have brought into being.

227
00:08:00,549 --> 00:08:02,999
- [Tom] Dr. Carlo
 Lombardi of Yonkers.

228
00:08:02,999 --> 00:08:05,485
[dog barking]

229
00:08:07,383 --> 00:08:09,627
- And I, Dr. Woof Woof Lombardi.

230
00:08:09,627 --> 00:08:12,353
- [Tom] Well, I can
 certainly see how, sleep!

231
00:08:14,079 --> 00:08:16,012
I need my worm
medicine, I need it now.

232
00:08:16,875 --> 00:08:18,118
- What's that?

233
00:08:18,118 --> 00:08:19,913
Grandpa Lombardi
 fell down a well?

234
00:08:19,913 --> 00:08:21,362
- [Tom] I'm sorry, Mr. Lombardi.

235
00:08:21,362 --> 00:08:22,743
I mistook you for someone else.

236
00:08:22,743 --> 00:08:24,365
I know my family owes you a lot.

237
00:08:25,539 --> 00:08:26,609
Look, you smell like spam.

238
00:08:26,609 --> 00:08:28,508
It was my mistake, my mistake.

239
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:29,992
God, I hate cats.

240
00:08:31,441 --> 00:08:33,547
I left a present for you in
 the front seat of your car.

241
00:08:36,274 --> 00:08:38,138
- [Mike] Top breeder
 Bat Masterson.

242
00:08:39,104 --> 00:08:40,796
- Hmm, Howard the Duck was here.

243
00:08:42,176 --> 00:08:44,075
- [Mike] I've got
 sand in my Derby.

244
00:08:47,768 --> 00:08:49,563
♪ Hey, hey, I'm the Monkee

245
00:08:49,563 --> 00:08:54,016
♪ People say I monkey around

246
00:08:54,016 --> 00:08:56,087
- Fun times at the
 Kennedy compound.

247
00:08:56,087 --> 00:08:58,503
- [Tom] Here you
 go, Mr. Trafficante.

248
00:08:58,503 --> 00:09:00,194
- Enjoying your weekend
with the idle rich?

249
00:09:00,194 --> 00:09:01,644
- [Tom] When does it start?

250
00:09:01,644 --> 00:09:04,578
- Pretty heady stuff for a
 professor of psychic research.

251
00:09:04,578 --> 00:09:06,062
- You sound a
 little disapproving.

252
00:09:06,062 --> 00:09:07,305
- Not at all.

253
00:09:07,305 --> 00:09:08,755
I just don't feel
 I belong in a world

254
00:09:08,755 --> 00:09:10,757
of yachts and racing stakes.

255
00:09:10,757 --> 00:09:14,312
Some of those tycoons in
 there, including your father.

256
00:09:14,312 --> 00:09:15,520
Kind of frightens me.

257
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,108
- Oh come now, this type
of life shouldn't be

258
00:09:17,108 --> 00:09:18,523
too hard to get used to.

259
00:09:18,523 --> 00:09:19,697
- Let's face it.

260
00:09:19,697 --> 00:09:21,388
I'm an Alloway farm boy
with a professorship

261
00:09:21,388 --> 00:09:23,148
at the university.

262
00:09:23,148 --> 00:09:25,634
But basically, a farm boy.

263
00:09:25,634 --> 00:09:27,946
I don't belong in all that.

264
00:09:27,946 --> 00:09:29,154
- Very well, then.

265
00:09:29,154 --> 00:09:30,604
We'll get you away
 from them for a while.

266
00:09:30,604 --> 00:09:32,226
A walk along the ocean'll do it.

267
00:09:33,296 --> 00:09:34,712
- I'd like that.
- But I don't know how.

268
00:09:34,712 --> 00:09:38,163
- I don't know how your fiance
 will react to that idea.

269
00:09:38,163 --> 00:09:41,132
- Oh, Bob, my ex-fiance?

270
00:09:41,132 --> 00:09:42,478
That makes quite a difference.

271
00:09:42,478 --> 00:09:43,410
- Come on, Ted.

272
00:09:43,410 --> 00:09:44,445
- You've got the backstory.

273
00:09:44,445 --> 00:09:45,412
Now run!

274
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,070
- [Tom] I'm ready
 for some football.

275
00:09:49,347 --> 00:09:52,005
[Mike muttering]

276
00:09:52,005 --> 00:09:55,180
- Oh, mafia goons and withered
 spinsters partying together.

277
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,597
- So that horrid blond
finally let you go, eh?

278
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,012
- [Tom] Hey, that's
 our daughter.

279
00:09:59,012 --> 00:10:01,773
- That horrid blond represents
 an investment portfolio

280
00:10:01,773 --> 00:10:03,568
of half a million bucks.

281
00:10:03,568 --> 00:10:04,534
Where's Dorothy?

282
00:10:04,534 --> 00:10:05,846
- She went for a walk with Ted.

283
00:10:05,846 --> 00:10:07,779
Oh, I wish she hadn't.

284
00:10:07,779 --> 00:10:09,298
- Why?

285
00:10:09,298 --> 00:10:11,852
- Dr. Lombardi said something
 terrible is going to happen

286
00:10:11,852 --> 00:10:13,474
along this part of
 the coast tonight.

287
00:10:13,474 --> 00:10:16,477
Some visitation from
 the occult world.

288
00:10:16,477 --> 00:10:17,824
- Oh, the occult world?

289
00:10:17,824 --> 00:10:19,446
- Oh no, really, seriously.

290
00:10:19,446 --> 00:10:20,274
You must meet him.

291
00:10:20,274 --> 00:10:21,793
He's wonderful.

292
00:10:21,793 --> 00:10:24,900
- Some women keep beds
or grow roses for kicks.

293
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:27,765
My wife supports
crack occultism.

294
00:10:27,765 --> 00:10:30,768
A couple of years ago it was
 that spiritualistic medium.

295
00:10:30,768 --> 00:10:35,324
Last year, swarmy something or
 other, and now Dr. Lombardi.

296
00:10:35,324 --> 00:10:37,084
- [ Tom] Oh, Professor Firefly.

297
00:10:37,084 --> 00:10:39,086
- So long as it amuses you.

298
00:10:39,086 --> 00:10:40,570
- No, seriously.

299
00:10:40,570 --> 00:10:43,643
He puts this girl
 into a deep trance,

300
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:46,231
and takes her back 300 years.

301
00:10:46,231 --> 00:10:48,648
Now she tells about
 her life in England.

302
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:50,684
I tell you, it's uncanny.

303
00:10:50,684 --> 00:10:53,066
- Yes, well.
 - I married Aunt Bee.

304
00:10:53,066 --> 00:10:55,309
- Looks pretty serious
between Dorothy and Ted.

305
00:10:55,309 --> 00:10:56,656
She's falling for him.

306
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,796
- I'm afraid it's
pretty one-sided so far.

307
00:10:58,796 --> 00:11:00,142
- Nonsense.

308
00:11:00,142 --> 00:11:01,764
If she wants him,
 she'll get him.

309
00:11:01,764 --> 00:11:06,079
What's the market price on
professors of psychic research?

310
00:11:06,079 --> 00:11:07,321
Not very high, I imagine.

311
00:11:07,321 --> 00:11:09,427
- [laughs] You goose.
 - You pheasant.

312
00:11:09,427 --> 00:11:12,085
- Mother's a little
 disappointed in you.

313
00:11:12,085 --> 00:11:13,673
She thought you'd
 liven up the party

314
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,778
with some of the
 tricks of your trade.

315
00:11:15,778 --> 00:11:19,506
You know, hypnotism,
 demonstrations of
 thought transference.

316
00:11:19,506 --> 00:11:20,749
- I know.

317
00:11:20,749 --> 00:11:23,337
She thought I'd make it
an age regression party.

318
00:11:23,337 --> 00:11:25,892
I told her that was Dr.
 Lombardi's field, not mine.

319
00:11:27,031 --> 00:11:28,584
- [Mike] I could use a Frogurt.

320
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:33,934
- The Fleet Street
 line of beachwear.

321
00:11:35,418 --> 00:11:36,903
- [Tom] Is this the Mr.
Kite everyone's always

322
00:11:36,903 --> 00:11:38,801
doing stuff for the benefit of?

323
00:11:38,801 --> 00:11:40,320
- [Mike] Paladin's beach home.

324
00:11:41,459 --> 00:11:43,806
- Smitty, Merv, you maniacs.

325
00:11:43,806 --> 00:11:45,670
- [Tom] Oh, it's
 Helen Keller's room.

326
00:11:48,397 --> 00:11:49,916
Hello, wall.

327
00:11:49,916 --> 00:11:52,573
- Make yourself at home, just
 looking at the wall here.

328
00:11:53,954 --> 00:11:55,956
- [Mike] Guys, are we
 still gonna watch the game?

329
00:11:57,682 --> 00:11:59,649
Damn cats.

330
00:11:59,649 --> 00:12:00,961
- [Tom] This is scary.

331
00:12:00,961 --> 00:12:02,756
I'm not gonna get
 any sleep tonight.

332
00:12:04,137 --> 00:12:06,070
- [Mike] Man with flaming
 swim fins did this.

333
00:12:09,798 --> 00:12:10,764
- Mayhem I can put up with.

334
00:12:10,764 --> 00:12:13,077
It's the damn dust I just...

335
00:12:14,561 --> 00:12:15,735
[dog barking]

336
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:16,632
- [Tom] Rin Tin
 Tin in Coming Home.

337
00:12:21,188 --> 00:12:23,156
Hey, you know
 where my socks are?

338
00:12:25,986 --> 00:12:27,160
- The death of Tyne Daly.

339
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,989
- He's an amazing man.

340
00:12:28,989 --> 00:12:30,025
Do you know him?

341
00:12:30,025 --> 00:12:31,578
- Quite well.

342
00:12:31,578 --> 00:12:33,614
He's challenged me
 publicly and privately

343
00:12:33,614 --> 00:12:36,203
to disprove the authenticity
 of his experiments.

344
00:12:36,203 --> 00:12:37,515
- [Tom] And to oil
 jockstrap wrestling.

345
00:12:37,515 --> 00:12:38,447
[dog barking]

346
00:12:38,447 --> 00:12:40,173
- That sounds like King's bark.

347
00:12:40,173 --> 00:12:41,657
- [Mike] Since it's King
running right at us,

348
00:12:41,657 --> 00:12:43,210
you're probably right.
 - Yeah.

349
00:12:46,524 --> 00:12:47,905
[dramatic music]

350
00:12:47,905 --> 00:12:52,012
- [Tom] I can't believe
I ate the whole thing.

351
00:12:52,012 --> 00:12:55,498
As your RA, I should warn
 you you're facing expulsion.

352
00:12:57,086 --> 00:12:58,847
- I'm going out for a
 sack of White Castles.

353
00:12:58,847 --> 00:12:59,709
You want anything?

354
00:12:59,709 --> 00:13:01,194
[dog barking]

355
00:13:01,194 --> 00:13:02,782
- [Tom] I just found out
my food is mostly rice.

356
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:04,404
Can I have some lamb, please?

357
00:13:05,577 --> 00:13:07,545
- Well what's the
 matter with him?

358
00:13:07,545 --> 00:13:08,373
- Maybe he's jealous of me.

359
00:13:08,373 --> 00:13:10,065
- Oh, that's weird.

360
00:13:10,065 --> 00:13:11,860
- You haven't given
 him cause to be, yet.

361
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:14,172
[dog barking]

362
00:13:14,172 --> 00:13:15,622
- I think I've made my point.

363
00:13:16,934 --> 00:13:18,452
- He wants us to follow him.

364
00:13:18,452 --> 00:13:19,799
- [Tom] Oh, gee,
do you think so?

365
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:21,490
Of course I want
 you to follow me.

366
00:13:23,319 --> 00:13:25,770
Well, I think I'll grab the
Boogie Board and hit some waves.

367
00:13:25,770 --> 00:13:27,289
- I hope to god we don't
see this guy in a thong

368
00:13:27,289 --> 00:13:28,669
before the movie's over.

369
00:13:30,016 --> 00:13:32,501
[dog barking]

370
00:13:33,882 --> 00:13:36,781
- [Mike] I'm going to tell Hobie
to stay away from the pier.

371
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,542
- That looked like
 Dr. Lombardi to me.

372
00:13:40,474 --> 00:13:41,855
- It was Dr. Lombardi.

373
00:13:41,855 --> 00:13:44,099
- And that sounds
 like King's bark.

374
00:13:44,099 --> 00:13:45,307
- [Mike] Now come here.

375
00:13:45,307 --> 00:13:46,204
I want to prove to you,
I'm not the only one

376
00:13:46,204 --> 00:13:47,619
who craps in the corner.

377
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:50,139
[dog barking]

378
00:13:50,139 --> 00:13:51,071
- [Tom] Huh, what's that boy?

379
00:13:51,071 --> 00:13:53,108
A four-year assumable mortgage?

380
00:13:53,108 --> 00:13:54,350
Let's go.

381
00:13:54,350 --> 00:13:55,731
- I think I might have
 killed some people

382
00:13:55,731 --> 00:13:57,595
and I'm feeling a
 little bad about it.

383
00:14:00,115 --> 00:14:01,737
- [Tom] Should I
wait here, or...

384
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:05,361
♪ Everybody is a starfish

385
00:14:05,361 --> 00:14:06,846
- Shazam, my pipe's gone.

386
00:14:08,675 --> 00:14:10,746
- [Tom] The Dallas
 Cowboys training camp.

387
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:13,162
King, what have you done here?

388
00:14:13,162 --> 00:14:14,267
King, kill outside.

389
00:14:14,267 --> 00:14:15,475
Outside, King!

390
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:19,030
- You're gonna hang
 for this, King.

391
00:14:23,276 --> 00:14:24,277
- Well, what is it?

392
00:14:24,277 --> 00:14:26,486
- Go on home and
call the police.

393
00:14:26,486 --> 00:14:27,521
- The police?

394
00:14:27,521 --> 00:14:28,902
- I'll wait here for them.

395
00:14:28,902 --> 00:14:29,869
Hurry up.

396
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:31,284
- King is the Scorpio Killer.

397
00:14:33,182 --> 00:14:35,081
- The only movie
 based on a lens flare.

398
00:14:35,081 --> 00:14:37,428
- Huh, I don't feel fresh.

399
00:14:38,912 --> 00:14:41,535
[upbeat music]

400
00:14:45,436 --> 00:14:46,886
- Never seen anything like it.

401
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:48,888
Neck's broken in two like
 a pile-driver hit her.

402
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:50,959
The man's too.
 - I suspect a pile-driver.

403
00:14:50,959 --> 00:14:53,616
- I've got $600 here.
 - That's 300 each.

404
00:14:53,616 --> 00:14:54,963
- That lets robbery out.

405
00:14:54,963 --> 00:14:55,825
- Hey.

406
00:14:57,310 --> 00:14:58,518
Here's something.

407
00:14:58,518 --> 00:15:00,451
- Of course you can say
that about anything.

408
00:15:00,451 --> 00:15:01,486
- A piece of seaweed.

409
00:15:03,109 --> 00:15:05,283
All the way to the door.
- Eisenhower, P.I..

410
00:15:05,283 --> 00:15:07,492
- The carpet's wet here.

411
00:15:07,492 --> 00:15:09,149
Might be a footprint.

412
00:15:09,149 --> 00:15:11,082
Go into the kitchen and see if
 there's any flour, will you?

413
00:15:11,082 --> 00:15:12,912
- Roll in it and
 pan fry yourself.

414
00:15:15,776 --> 00:15:17,675
- You willing to
 swear you saw Lombardi

415
00:15:17,675 --> 00:15:19,366
coming out of this house?

416
00:15:19,366 --> 00:15:20,195
- Course.

417
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:23,163
- Who wants cookies?

418
00:15:23,163 --> 00:15:24,509
I'm going to make
 some Toll House.

419
00:15:26,787 --> 00:15:28,479
- [Mike] By the way,
why do we do this, Earl?

420
00:15:28,479 --> 00:15:29,894
- [Tom] Detective's
 handbook number one.

421
00:15:29,894 --> 00:15:31,344
Chuck flour and blow on it.

422
00:15:33,553 --> 00:15:35,279
- What'd make a
 footprint like that?

423
00:15:35,279 --> 00:15:36,521
- Bill Walton?

424
00:15:36,521 --> 00:15:37,798
- Clever man could
 have forged it.

425
00:15:37,798 --> 00:15:39,835
- Do you think a human
 could have done this?

426
00:15:39,835 --> 00:15:41,354
- No, I think a
 mudskipper did it.

427
00:15:41,354 --> 00:15:43,839
- Oh, I almost forgot
 about your firm belief

428
00:15:43,839 --> 00:15:46,738
in Lombardi's black
magic and occult powers.

429
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:47,774
- It's not me.

430
00:15:47,774 --> 00:15:48,602
It's my wife.

431
00:15:48,602 --> 00:15:49,845
She swears by him.

432
00:15:49,845 --> 00:15:51,985
- What did he say was
coming to roam among us?

433
00:15:51,985 --> 00:15:52,952
- He said, "Sleep!"

434
00:15:54,781 --> 00:15:57,611
- The first life-form
of someone living today.

435
00:15:57,611 --> 00:15:59,613
Over a million years old.

436
00:15:59,613 --> 00:16:01,408
- Strom Thurmond?

437
00:16:01,408 --> 00:16:04,239
- You see, doctor, that's
 how civilized we are.

438
00:16:04,239 --> 00:16:05,930
Scratch the veneer
 and what do you find?

439
00:16:05,930 --> 00:16:08,968
A whole car-load of
 superstitions waiting
 to be catered to.

440
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:12,592
Vampires, witchcraft,
supernatural creatures.

441
00:16:12,592 --> 00:16:14,076
Being brought back
 from the past.

442
00:16:14,076 --> 00:16:14,939
M Just patting my own arm.

443
00:16:14,939 --> 00:16:16,113
I'm not in this scene.

444
00:16:16,113 --> 00:16:17,390
- He's got a lot of
people listening to him.

445
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:18,184
- It's not me.

446
00:16:18,184 --> 00:16:19,392
It's my wife.

447
00:16:19,392 --> 00:16:20,220
- All right.

448
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:21,497
It's your wife.

449
00:16:21,497 --> 00:16:23,189
- Yeah, like somebody
 lays with you anyway.

450
00:16:23,189 --> 00:16:24,397
- You willing to
 identify Lombardi now?

451
00:16:24,397 --> 00:16:25,881
Make things a lot simpler.

452
00:16:25,881 --> 00:16:27,262
- Sure.

453
00:16:27,262 --> 00:16:28,573
- You wait here
 for the lab boys.

454
00:16:28,573 --> 00:16:29,574
And I want pictures.

455
00:16:29,574 --> 00:16:30,506
Plenty of them.

456
00:16:30,506 --> 00:16:31,749
- You gonna leave me alone here?

457
00:16:31,749 --> 00:16:33,371
It's not like it was
 an ordinary stiff.

458
00:16:33,371 --> 00:16:34,959
I can take that
 seven days a week.

459
00:16:34,959 --> 00:16:35,891
- Come on.

460
00:16:35,891 --> 00:16:38,169
- But, it might come back.

461
00:16:38,169 --> 00:16:40,240
- But it's not you
 that is superstitious.

462
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,414
It's your wife who's
 the gullible one.

463
00:16:41,414 --> 00:16:43,795
- I'm a flaky little
 detective elf.

464
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:49,732
- [Mike] Brooklyn, California.

465
00:16:52,045 --> 00:16:54,047
- [Tom] Get your
 bags of rat filth.

466
00:16:55,186 --> 00:16:57,016
Step right up, I'll
touch you for a quarter.

467
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:59,087
Come on.
 - Rat filth.

468
00:16:59,087 --> 00:17:01,020
Hey, I found another
 dirty diaper.

469
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,505
- We'll make you, break you,
 set you on a farm out West.

470
00:17:03,505 --> 00:17:04,333
10 cents.

471
00:17:04,333 --> 00:17:05,265
Yes, siree.

472
00:17:05,265 --> 00:17:06,680
Hello, Lombardi.

473
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:07,474
Lousy night.

474
00:17:07,474 --> 00:17:08,303
No business at all.

475
00:17:09,166 --> 00:17:10,960
- I find it very pleasant.

476
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:13,170
- I heard a scream from your
 place about 15 minutes ago.

477
00:17:13,170 --> 00:17:14,688
I thought it was Andrea.

478
00:17:14,688 --> 00:17:16,483
I ran over to check up,
 see if she was in trouble.

479
00:17:16,483 --> 00:17:18,175
- I told you to keep
 away from there.

480
00:17:18,175 --> 00:17:20,039
- I knew her long
 before you did, doc.

481
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:22,006
I knew her when she was
a carnival follower.

482
00:17:22,006 --> 00:17:24,146
Every time we hit a town
 she'd be there waiting for us.

483
00:17:24,146 --> 00:17:25,906
- So she's a carnival preceder.

484
00:17:25,906 --> 00:17:27,632
- I've asked you to forget that.

485
00:17:27,632 --> 00:17:29,082
- [Tom] Have we met?

486
00:17:29,082 --> 00:17:30,325
- Well, anyway, I heard the
 screams, so I went over.

487
00:17:30,325 --> 00:17:31,981
The back door was
 open, I went in.

488
00:17:31,981 --> 00:17:33,155
She was out cold.

489
00:17:34,294 --> 00:17:35,640
How do you keep her
 under like that?

490
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:36,572
I thought she was dead.

491
00:17:36,572 --> 00:17:38,160
I was going to call the cops.

492
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:40,024
- It's so tiresome
 having to warn you

493
00:17:40,024 --> 00:17:42,061
to mind your own business.

494
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:43,752
So very tiresome.

495
00:17:43,752 --> 00:17:46,168
- Well, I'm naturally curious.

496
00:17:46,168 --> 00:17:47,687
Poor kid, she was out cold.

497
00:17:48,550 --> 00:17:49,758
What's it all about, doc?

498
00:17:49,758 --> 00:17:50,793
Why do you keep her
 under like that?

499
00:17:50,793 --> 00:17:52,071
- Alfie.

500
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:54,245
- I have an idea
 you'll find out soon.

501
00:17:56,109 --> 00:17:58,353
- [Tom] Was it something I
said at breakfast this morning?

502
00:18:00,148 --> 00:18:01,735
See his lecture series.

503
00:18:01,735 --> 00:18:04,566
Let a smile be his calling card.

504
00:18:04,566 --> 00:18:06,878
- Author, lecturer,
 choreographer.

505
00:18:07,983 --> 00:18:10,123
- [Tom] Endorsed
by King the dog.

506
00:18:10,123 --> 00:18:11,400
- [Mike] I barked my ass off.

507
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,678
You'll laugh, you'll
 growl, you'll pee.

508
00:18:13,678 --> 00:18:16,888
- See him perform live with
 his band, Thunkersaurus.

509
00:18:18,442 --> 00:18:20,547
- [Tom] Damn, I left
 the woman plugged in.

510
00:18:23,930 --> 00:18:25,207
- [Mike] This guy
 leaves grease stains

511
00:18:25,207 --> 00:18:27,278
in the air as he walks.

512
00:18:27,278 --> 00:18:29,384
- I come home from a
 hard day of skulking

513
00:18:29,384 --> 00:18:30,557
and the place isn't cleaned?

514
00:18:30,557 --> 00:18:32,214
You're just laying there
thinking of bonbons.

515
00:18:32,214 --> 00:18:34,492
- You're in a deep
 sleep, Andrea.

516
00:18:35,804 --> 00:18:37,426
A very deep sleep.

517
00:18:37,426 --> 00:18:39,152
- [Mike] I was.

518
00:18:39,152 --> 00:18:41,327
- I'll touch you, and
 slowly you will wake.

519
00:18:41,327 --> 00:18:43,467
- [Tom] And you'll get
 me some damn dinner.

520
00:18:44,744 --> 00:18:47,816
[Crow slurping]

521
00:18:47,816 --> 00:18:49,714
Well, I'd better
repaint my head.

522
00:18:54,616 --> 00:18:56,721
- Someone ripped off
 our lawn gnome again.

523
00:19:02,071 --> 00:19:06,179
Yeah, she's dreaming of old
 carnivals she's been to.

524
00:19:06,179 --> 00:19:08,181
- [Mike] There any
 turkey sausages left?

525
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:11,150
♪ There'll be creatures over

526
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,634
♪ The white cliffs of Dover

527
00:19:12,634 --> 00:19:15,223
- Well, I got to go bleed
 the sprinklers, I don't know.

528
00:19:19,330 --> 00:19:21,643
- [Mike] Oh honey, please
 don't spend another Christmas

529
00:19:21,643 --> 00:19:23,472
passed out on the couch.

530
00:19:23,472 --> 00:19:25,336
- Now you'll come
 back to me, Andrea.

531
00:19:26,820 --> 00:19:28,684
You'll feel refreshed.

532
00:19:28,684 --> 00:19:30,169
You'll remember nothing.

533
00:19:30,169 --> 00:19:31,308
- [Tom] You'll remember
how to go potty

534
00:19:31,308 --> 00:19:32,999
and chew and stuff, but...

535
00:19:34,483 --> 00:19:37,106
- [Mike] He's like an
 unattractive Slim Whitman.

536
00:19:37,106 --> 00:19:39,143
- That's great, Mesmer,
but you left jelly

537
00:19:39,143 --> 00:19:40,075
all over the cutting
 board this morning.

538
00:19:40,075 --> 00:19:41,525
- [Tom] I've got to go levitate

539
00:19:41,525 --> 00:19:43,182
over to Denny's for my shift.

540
00:19:44,044 --> 00:19:45,701
- What time is it?

541
00:19:45,701 --> 00:19:46,978
- Shortly after midnight.

542
00:19:46,978 --> 00:19:49,464
- Don't let it all
 hang down, please.

543
00:19:49,464 --> 00:19:53,330
- You've had me in a deep
hypnosis for more than an hour.

544
00:19:53,330 --> 00:19:54,883
I asked you not to do that.

545
00:19:55,884 --> 00:19:57,679
- Well, you were tired.

546
00:19:57,679 --> 00:19:59,922
You needed the rest.

547
00:19:59,922 --> 00:20:02,649
- I need to get away from here.

548
00:20:02,649 --> 00:20:03,478
Away from you.

549
00:20:05,065 --> 00:20:06,135
- [Mike] Can I come?

550
00:20:06,135 --> 00:20:07,585
- I hate this place.

551
00:20:08,517 --> 00:20:10,105
I hate the sound of the ocean.

552
00:20:11,865 --> 00:20:13,281
I hate you.

553
00:20:13,281 --> 00:20:16,007
- [Tom] I can't help but
 feel that was directed at me.

554
00:20:17,561 --> 00:20:19,666
- I didn't mean I
 hate you in a bad way.

555
00:20:21,910 --> 00:20:23,774
- [Tom] Anyone call
 about the Charger?

556
00:20:26,086 --> 00:20:27,916
- You'll never leave me.

557
00:20:27,916 --> 00:20:29,435
You can't.

558
00:20:29,435 --> 00:20:30,850
- I will.

559
00:20:30,850 --> 00:20:31,885
Someday I will.

560
00:20:32,714 --> 00:20:33,991
Soon.

561
00:20:33,991 --> 00:20:35,406
- [Mike] You want
 to make some nachos?

562
00:20:35,406 --> 00:20:37,546
As long as I'm alive
 I'll possess you.

563
00:20:37,546 --> 00:20:39,099
- I should bag those leaves.

564
00:20:39,099 --> 00:20:42,655
- There's something beyond
yourself that makes you need me.

565
00:20:42,655 --> 00:20:44,657
- You've taken my
 soul away from me.

566
00:20:44,657 --> 00:20:48,108
- [Tom] You told me to take
 it so you wouldn't overuse it.

567
00:20:48,108 --> 00:20:51,008
[knocking on door]

568
00:20:51,008 --> 00:20:52,561
- The door is open.

569
00:20:52,561 --> 00:20:53,355
Come in.

570
00:20:55,495 --> 00:20:58,257
- [Mike] Can we get
 two seats together?

571
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,085
- [Tom] Hi, Max.

572
00:21:00,776 --> 00:21:03,123
- May I suggest a
 size up from that?

573
00:21:03,123 --> 00:21:04,228
- Yeah.

574
00:21:04,228 --> 00:21:05,471
- I'm Lieutenant James.

575
00:21:05,471 --> 00:21:06,713
- Hello.

576
00:21:06,713 --> 00:21:07,887
- [Mike] This is Timmy.

577
00:21:11,339 --> 00:21:13,099
- Dr. Erickson?
- Breast?

578
00:21:13,099 --> 00:21:14,549
- Yeah?

579
00:21:14,549 --> 00:21:16,551
- Is this the man you saw coming
out of the Jefferson house?

580
00:21:16,551 --> 00:21:18,000
- Boobies, exactly.
 - Yeah.

581
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,968
- No doubt in your mind?

582
00:21:19,968 --> 00:21:20,934
- No.

583
00:21:20,934 --> 00:21:22,867
He knows me quite well.

584
00:21:22,867 --> 00:21:25,594
I've been trying to interest
 him in my work for some time.

585
00:21:25,594 --> 00:21:27,320
You don't deny you were
in the Jefferson house

586
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:30,116
approximately 15
 minutes after 11?

587
00:21:30,116 --> 00:21:31,324
- Not at all.

588
00:21:31,324 --> 00:21:32,808
- Well, that closes
 the investigation.

589
00:21:32,808 --> 00:21:35,432
- I won't need you any
 longer, doctor, thank you.

590
00:21:35,432 --> 00:21:36,295
Nor you, miss.

591
00:21:38,435 --> 00:21:41,507
- [Tom] Wow, it's the federal
 witness seduction program.

592
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:44,337
- Sleep?

593
00:21:44,337 --> 00:21:45,165
Sleep?

594
00:21:47,478 --> 00:21:48,514
- [Mike] You want
 to go home and play?

595
00:21:48,514 --> 00:21:49,756
I got a box of men.

596
00:21:49,756 --> 00:21:50,826
- What's it all about?

597
00:21:52,449 --> 00:21:55,210
- Maybe we can talk about
 it over a cup of coffee.

598
00:21:55,210 --> 00:21:56,453
- I'd like that.

599
00:21:56,453 --> 00:21:58,386
- Would you like a C-cup
or a D-cup of coffee?

600
00:21:59,766 --> 00:22:02,182
So, you go to carnival locations
and wait for them, huh?

601
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:08,257
- [Mike] Look into
 my oily T-zone.

602
00:22:09,638 --> 00:22:12,261
- I can't go with you.
 - I'm not a coffee achiever.

603
00:22:13,918 --> 00:22:16,024
And he ducks out of the screen.

604
00:22:16,024 --> 00:22:17,681
[Servo laughs]
 - Bye.

605
00:22:17,681 --> 00:22:19,959
- [Mike] Guess the
 stain and win a prize.

606
00:22:19,959 --> 00:22:20,787
- Oh.

607
00:22:21,926 --> 00:22:23,480
- You say you knew
 they were dead

608
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:25,344
the minute you
 saw the open door.

609
00:22:25,344 --> 00:22:27,242
- Yeah, see?
 - Yes, pity.

610
00:22:27,242 --> 00:22:28,726
Nice young couple.

611
00:22:30,210 --> 00:22:32,454
She came out of the ocean,
 just as I said she would.

612
00:22:32,454 --> 00:22:33,697
And she'll come again.

613
00:22:33,697 --> 00:22:35,664
- Look, I'm not a
 paying customer.

614
00:22:35,664 --> 00:22:37,356
I'm a police officer.

615
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,530
She comes from the
 beginning of time.

616
00:22:39,530 --> 00:22:41,360
Huge and indestructible.

617
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,637
- Thank you.

618
00:22:42,637 --> 00:22:44,811
- And I'm the force
 that gives her life.

619
00:22:44,811 --> 00:22:47,366
All I know, you were seen
 coming out of that house

620
00:22:47,366 --> 00:22:49,437
leaving two corpses behind you.

621
00:22:49,437 --> 00:22:51,611
And the occult world
 notwithstanding,

622
00:22:51,611 --> 00:22:53,717
I think I'll take you
 downtown and wait till

623
00:22:53,717 --> 00:22:54,994
the reports come in.

624
00:22:54,994 --> 00:22:56,375
- I can tell you what
 the reports will say.

625
00:22:56,375 --> 00:22:57,652
- They'll say "Sleep!"

626
00:22:57,652 --> 00:22:59,585
- That no living
 thing killed them.

627
00:22:59,585 --> 00:23:01,172
- Yeah, I know.

628
00:23:01,172 --> 00:23:03,934
It was a materialization
 of the prehistoric female.

629
00:23:03,934 --> 00:23:07,075
A transmigration of the
soul of a living woman,

630
00:23:07,075 --> 00:23:08,628
into her first life body.

631
00:23:08,628 --> 00:23:10,941
- Save it, save it for downtown.

632
00:23:12,218 --> 00:23:15,946
[doors whirring and closing]

633
00:23:23,056 --> 00:23:24,541
- Hey Mike, there you are.

634
00:23:24,541 --> 00:23:27,129
I had an idea and I wanted to
 run it by a totally average,

635
00:23:27,129 --> 00:23:32,100
unspectacular, not overly-bright
consumer, and here you are.

636
00:23:32,825 --> 00:23:34,343
- Yeah, sure Crow.

637
00:23:34,343 --> 00:23:35,172
- Good, hey, give me that
 thing under there will you?

638
00:23:35,172 --> 00:23:36,484
- Yeah, mm-hmm.

639
00:23:36,484 --> 00:23:39,348
- It's my Tickle Me
 Carlo Lombardi doll.

640
00:23:39,348 --> 00:23:40,419
- Oh, wow.

641
00:23:40,419 --> 00:23:41,903
What the?

642
00:23:41,903 --> 00:23:44,423
- Yeah, it's just like the
 lovable Tickle Me Elmo doll.

643
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:46,701
Only it's Carlo Lombardi.

644
00:23:46,701 --> 00:23:47,529
- What?

645
00:23:47,529 --> 00:23:49,048
Why?

646
00:23:49,048 --> 00:23:50,567
- Oh that's a lot of little
 boys, and it's a reaction

647
00:23:50,567 --> 00:23:53,293
to dolls, but you'll grow
 to love it as you take it

648
00:23:53,293 --> 00:23:55,157
into your room, perhaps prop it

649
00:23:55,157 --> 00:23:57,021
next to your bed as you sleep.

650
00:23:57,021 --> 00:23:58,437
He'll watch over you.

651
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:00,956
He's Dr. Carlo Lombardi.

652
00:24:00,956 --> 00:24:01,854
- Crow, why you make a doll?

653
00:24:01,854 --> 00:24:04,684
- Go ahead, Mike, tickle him.

654
00:24:04,684 --> 00:24:06,790
- Oh, I think
 you'd better, Mike.

655
00:24:06,790 --> 00:24:10,449
Tickle Me Carlo Lombardi
doesn't like to be disappointed.

656
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:12,623
- Well, just to be safe, okay.

657
00:24:12,623 --> 00:24:13,762
- That's right.
[dolls laughs]

658
00:24:13,762 --> 00:24:17,110
Tickle Me Carlo
Lombardi is your friend.

659
00:24:17,110 --> 00:24:18,318
Forever.

660
00:24:18,318 --> 00:24:19,734
[doll laughs]

661
00:24:19,734 --> 00:24:23,082
Yeah, and I made him sticky
 so he's even more fun.

662
00:24:23,082 --> 00:24:25,256
You can feed him the
 special baby food

663
00:24:25,256 --> 00:24:28,190
included and in a
 few minutes change

664
00:24:28,190 --> 00:24:30,469
Tickle Me Carlo
 Lombardi's daidie.

665
00:24:30,469 --> 00:24:33,437
- No, no!
 - And there's a song too.

666
00:24:33,437 --> 00:24:35,991
♪ Who's that fat little
funny little doll ♪

667
00:24:35,991 --> 00:24:38,684
♪ It's Tickle Me
Carlo Lombardi ♪

668
00:24:38,684 --> 00:24:41,549
♪ Whose little diaper needs
 a good little change ♪

669
00:24:41,549 --> 00:24:44,206
♪ It's Tickle Me
Carlo Lombardi ♪

670
00:24:44,206 --> 00:24:46,208
Tickle Me Carlo Lombardi
 and Tickle Me Carlo Lombardi

671
00:24:46,208 --> 00:24:47,416
sold separately.

672
00:24:47,416 --> 00:24:49,315
[doll laughs]

673
00:24:49,315 --> 00:24:51,662
You know, that thing's
 kind of creepy.

674
00:24:51,662 --> 00:24:52,939
No, I don't think it'll work.

675
00:24:52,939 --> 00:24:54,285
You can have that
 doll though, Mike.

676
00:24:54,285 --> 00:24:56,495
I'm done with it, thank you.

677
00:24:56,495 --> 00:24:59,532
[doll laughs]

678
00:24:59,532 --> 00:25:02,121
[upbeat music]

679
00:25:05,883 --> 00:25:07,126
- [Mike] Huh, will
 you look at that?

680
00:25:07,126 --> 00:25:09,887
Despite all his money,
Mr. Drysdale eats alone.

681
00:25:09,887 --> 00:25:11,268
- Where's my shirred eggs?

682
00:25:11,268 --> 00:25:13,891
[dog barking]

683
00:25:13,891 --> 00:25:15,375
- [Tom] Works every time.

684
00:25:15,375 --> 00:25:18,482
- That dog, it gives
 me the jitters.

685
00:25:18,482 --> 00:25:21,830
I get a nervous Adam's apple,
 and that makes my tie unfold.

686
00:25:21,830 --> 00:25:23,383
- Inspired by Balki.

687
00:25:23,383 --> 00:25:24,661
- Morning, gentlemen.
 - Morning, Ted.

688
00:25:24,661 --> 00:25:26,283
Dorothy will be
 down in a minute.

689
00:25:26,283 --> 00:25:27,215
- Dorothy can't.

690
00:25:27,215 --> 00:25:28,423
I killed her.

691
00:25:28,423 --> 00:25:29,355
- I'm certainly not
 too popular with

692
00:25:29,355 --> 00:25:30,494
that member of your family.

693
00:25:32,047 --> 00:25:34,394
- Take him to the kitchen and
 get him something to eat, huh?

694
00:25:34,394 --> 00:25:36,293
- The last time I took
 him to the kitchen,

695
00:25:36,293 --> 00:25:37,950
he nearly had the cook.

696
00:25:37,950 --> 00:25:39,158
- Thank you very much.

697
00:25:39,158 --> 00:25:40,159
Was so stupid.
- Come on, dog.

698
00:25:40,159 --> 00:25:42,541
[dog barking]

699
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:43,472
- Oh god, I am dead.

700
00:25:43,472 --> 00:25:44,543
My carotid artery.

701
00:25:45,405 --> 00:25:47,787
Racket's really heavy today.

702
00:25:47,787 --> 00:25:49,271
- Carnelli arrives at 10.

703
00:25:49,271 --> 00:25:50,203
- Good.

704
00:25:50,203 --> 00:25:51,515
Makes your men get up early.

705
00:25:51,515 --> 00:25:53,275
Shows he's aggressive,
 wants to get ahead.

706
00:25:53,275 --> 00:25:54,518
- Damn Jerries at it again.

707
00:25:54,518 --> 00:25:56,727
- You give me too much
 credit, Mr. Chappel.

708
00:25:56,727 --> 00:26:00,179
- This Jefferson thing
last night, pretty grim.

709
00:26:01,594 --> 00:26:03,562
Kept them all buzzing for a
 while after Dorothy came home.

710
00:26:03,562 --> 00:26:05,184
- I'm over here, sir.

711
00:26:05,184 --> 00:26:06,461
- It's surprising
 how many of them

712
00:26:06,461 --> 00:26:08,912
think that Lombardi had
something to do with it.

713
00:26:08,912 --> 00:26:10,741
The whole gang's been
 down to see his show.

714
00:26:10,741 --> 00:26:11,949
- Sorry, looked at you.

715
00:26:11,949 --> 00:26:13,572
- Chappel tried to bully
me into going along.

716
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:16,954
- Damn wigwags.

717
00:26:16,954 --> 00:26:18,646
- Take a look at
that front page.

718
00:26:18,646 --> 00:26:21,131
- God ailing, still holds on.

719
00:26:21,131 --> 00:26:23,133
Let me get my welding
 glasses on here.

720
00:26:26,792 --> 00:26:28,517
- I play a little
 game every morning.

721
00:26:28,517 --> 00:26:31,590
I call it my front page game.
 - Sure you do.

722
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:34,247
- I'm getting a little old
 to play most of the others.

723
00:26:34,247 --> 00:26:35,317
I'm a limp noodle.

724
00:26:36,525 --> 00:26:37,734
- I read the front
 page every morning

725
00:26:37,734 --> 00:26:39,149
and see if I can pick
 out an item or two

726
00:26:39,149 --> 00:26:41,047
that will make me
 a lot of money.

727
00:26:41,047 --> 00:26:43,671
Surprising how often
 it's worked out.

728
00:26:43,671 --> 00:26:44,982
You ever try it?

729
00:26:44,982 --> 00:26:46,397
- No, I can't say I have.

730
00:26:46,397 --> 00:26:48,434
- Can the She Creature
 begin killing now?

731
00:26:48,434 --> 00:26:50,505
- You read about the
 Jefferson murder?

732
00:26:50,505 --> 00:26:51,748
- Yes.

733
00:26:51,748 --> 00:26:54,267
- There's a million
 dollar idea in that.

734
00:26:54,267 --> 00:26:55,406
Last paragraph.

735
00:26:55,406 --> 00:26:56,615
Read it.

736
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:58,617
- Sell something for
 a million dollars.

737
00:26:59,756 --> 00:27:01,585
- "One baffling
 aspect of the case

738
00:27:01,585 --> 00:27:04,899
concerns Dr. Carlo
 Lombardi, carnival hypnotist

739
00:27:04,899 --> 00:27:06,210
and prognosticator."

740
00:27:06,210 --> 00:27:07,626
- That's the plot summary.

741
00:27:07,626 --> 00:27:09,593
- "Only last week, he
 predicted that such a murder

742
00:27:09,593 --> 00:27:12,838
would take place, describing
 it with grisly accuracy.

743
00:27:12,838 --> 00:27:15,219
He was questioned by the
police, but not held."

744
00:27:15,219 --> 00:27:17,566
- Molly Ivins can't say that.

745
00:27:17,566 --> 00:27:19,430
- You see a fortune in that?

746
00:27:19,430 --> 00:27:20,846
- Yes.
- Oh, wait, no.

747
00:27:20,846 --> 00:27:22,433
- Yes, and it's
 right up your alley.

748
00:27:22,433 --> 00:27:23,434
- Ouch.

749
00:27:23,434 --> 00:27:25,644
- And yours is a
wedding present.

750
00:27:25,644 --> 00:27:26,748
- You're serious, aren't you?

751
00:27:26,748 --> 00:27:28,301
- Couldn't be more so.

752
00:27:28,301 --> 00:27:30,649
We'll take this two-bit
local sideshow man

753
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:33,444
and build him into the
 biggest thing in the country.

754
00:27:33,444 --> 00:27:36,309
Build him up until his
 name's on everyone's lips.

755
00:27:36,309 --> 00:27:37,932
Lombardi books.

756
00:27:37,932 --> 00:27:40,659
Syndicated columns,
 lectures, television shows.

757
00:27:40,659 --> 00:27:42,177
- Cheese, a line of underwear.

758
00:27:42,177 --> 00:27:43,523
- This prediction of his
 is worth a million dollars

759
00:27:43,523 --> 00:27:45,664
and you and I can do it.

760
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:46,803
- Where do I fit in?

761
00:27:46,803 --> 00:27:47,735
- You don't.

762
00:27:47,735 --> 00:27:49,184
I bought you out already.

763
00:27:49,184 --> 00:27:51,946
- You can give him the
 stamp of authenticity.

764
00:27:51,946 --> 00:27:54,673
Dr. Erickson, psychic
research specialist says

765
