00:54:53,842 --> 00:54:56,223
- I've been thinking of
your work, Dr. Lombardi.

1525
00:54:56,223 --> 00:54:58,674
I think it requires
 some serious study.

1526
00:54:58,674 --> 00:55:00,227
- Oh, good, I'm delighted.

1527
00:55:00,227 --> 00:55:01,436
- In fact I'm radiant.

1528
00:55:01,436 --> 00:55:02,575
- I want to talk
 to your assistant.

1529
00:55:02,575 --> 00:55:03,369
- Of course.

1530
00:55:03,369 --> 00:55:04,749
Any time you wish.

1531
00:55:04,749 --> 00:55:05,992
Perhaps this morning.

1532
00:55:05,992 --> 00:55:07,545
- Fine, you set it
 up for me, then.

1533
00:55:07,545 --> 00:55:10,030
- Oh, by the way, I
 backed up the toilet.

1534
00:55:10,030 --> 00:55:11,273
Sorry about that.

1535
00:55:11,273 --> 00:55:13,344
- Cracking good toast
this morning, eh, what?

1536
00:55:13,344 --> 00:55:16,002
- You really poured it on
 last night, didn't you?

1537
00:55:16,002 --> 00:55:18,798
That She Creature stuff was
 a stroke of sheer genius.

1538
00:55:20,213 --> 00:55:22,422
Everyone let out like the
 plague was after them.

1539
00:55:22,422 --> 00:55:23,768
They'll be talking it up today.

1540
00:55:23,768 --> 00:55:25,287
- Yes, I've no doubt of that.

1541
00:55:25,287 --> 00:55:26,530
- Hmm.

1542
00:55:26,530 --> 00:55:27,496
And that stuff on the
 pier the other night,

1543
00:55:27,496 --> 00:55:28,911
the way you tied in with that.

1544
00:55:28,911 --> 00:55:31,535
- That was a very fortunate
 coincidence for us.

1545
00:55:31,535 --> 00:55:33,088
- Yes, very.

1546
00:55:33,088 --> 00:55:35,055
- By the way, I shall require
 more suitable living quarters.

1547
00:55:35,055 --> 00:55:37,057
Shall I stay here
 till I find them?

1548
00:55:37,057 --> 00:55:38,058
Thank you very much.

1549
00:55:40,406 --> 00:55:42,269
- It's Carlo Kato
 Lombardi Kaelin.

1550
00:55:44,444 --> 00:55:46,377
- Ah, the Exxon Valdez beach.

1551
00:55:50,485 --> 00:55:51,348
- Is this felt?

1552
00:55:51,348 --> 00:55:53,073
It is now. [laughs]

1553
00:55:53,073 --> 00:55:54,178
- Thank you for meeting me here

1554
00:55:54,178 --> 00:55:55,869
at the sound stage by the beach.

1555
00:55:55,869 --> 00:55:57,492
- What are you doing out here?

1556
00:55:57,492 --> 00:55:59,010
- Looking bleary and waxen.

1557
00:55:59,010 --> 00:56:00,598
- Trying to get away from you.

1558
00:56:00,598 --> 00:56:02,669
For a few minutes, anyway.

1559
00:56:02,669 --> 00:56:04,361
- Not even for a minute.

1560
00:56:04,361 --> 00:56:05,914
- Ever heard of personal space?

1561
00:56:06,811 --> 00:56:08,226
- I'll never be free of you.

1562
00:56:09,780 --> 00:56:11,091
Why did it have to be me?

1563
00:56:12,265 --> 00:56:13,473
- Sleep?

1564
00:56:13,473 --> 00:56:16,373
- It was meant to be.
- Your earwigs are back.

1565
00:56:16,373 --> 00:56:17,960
- If you knew how I hated it.

1566
00:56:17,960 --> 00:56:19,168
Hated you.

1567
00:56:19,168 --> 00:56:20,687
- You're falling in love
with me, aren't you?

1568
00:56:22,275 --> 00:56:23,759
- You will do as I say.

1569
00:56:23,759 --> 00:56:26,659
- You will not go to the
prom with Tim Hariboth.

1570
00:56:26,659 --> 00:56:27,453
- Come here.

1571
00:56:28,557 --> 00:56:30,076
- Okay, I'm under your command,

1572
00:56:30,076 --> 00:56:31,767
but do you have
 to micromanage me?

1573
00:56:32,665 --> 00:56:33,976
- You're asleep, Andrea.

1574
00:56:33,976 --> 00:56:36,116
- Oh, cut the crap!

1575
00:56:36,116 --> 00:56:37,739
- You can hear what I'm saying.

1576
00:56:39,223 --> 00:56:40,466
You can understand me.

1577
00:56:40,466 --> 00:56:42,399
- She used a little too
much false eyelash glue.

1578
00:56:42,399 --> 00:56:45,022
- Yeah.
 - You're relaxed, Andrea.

1579
00:56:45,022 --> 00:56:46,299
- I bet he does this
 whenever he needs

1580
00:56:46,299 --> 00:56:47,749
to borrow a couple
 of bucks from her.

1581
00:56:47,749 --> 00:56:51,546
- I can't hear you, Mayo-naise.

1582
00:56:51,546 --> 00:56:53,858
- Dr. Erickson wishes
 to talk to you.

1583
00:56:53,858 --> 00:56:55,101
- He wants to level your eyes.

1584
00:56:55,101 --> 00:56:57,137
- He's going to try
 to hypnotize you.

1585
00:56:57,137 --> 00:56:58,345
You must resist him.

1586
00:56:58,345 --> 00:56:59,657
You will resist him.

1587
00:56:59,657 --> 00:57:01,314
- As effectively as
 I'm resisting you?

1588
00:57:01,314 --> 00:57:03,212
- He is our enemy.
 - He's a Commie.

1589
00:57:03,212 --> 00:57:05,629
- He is trying to destroy us.

1590
00:57:05,629 --> 00:57:06,837
You understand?

1591
00:57:06,837 --> 00:57:09,218
- He's jealous of our
 dynamite roadshow.

1592
00:57:09,218 --> 00:57:11,669
- Beauty like yours
 must not be destroyed.

1593
00:57:13,050 --> 00:57:14,258
It belongs to me.

1594
00:57:14,258 --> 00:57:16,571
- Is he attempting a
docking procedure here?

1595
00:57:16,571 --> 00:57:18,642
- I love you, Andrea.

1596
00:57:18,642 --> 00:57:20,229
And you love me too.

1597
00:57:20,229 --> 00:57:22,128
[Mike groans]

1598
00:57:22,128 --> 00:57:25,683
- He has the raw sex appeal
 of Caspar Weinberger.

1599
00:57:25,683 --> 00:57:26,581
- Say it.

1600
00:57:26,581 --> 00:57:27,685
[Mike groans]

1601
00:57:27,685 --> 00:57:29,238
- No!

1602
00:57:29,238 --> 00:57:30,516
- She should get a Purple
 Heart for doing this role.

1603
00:57:30,516 --> 00:57:32,138
- I hate you with all my heart.

1604
00:57:32,138 --> 00:57:33,070
- Really?

1605
00:57:33,070 --> 00:57:33,795
Then we're to be married.

1606
00:57:35,072 --> 00:57:37,005
- I could make your
 grovel in the dirt.

1607
00:57:38,213 --> 00:57:39,973
I can turn you into
 Elizabeth Wetherby.

1608
00:57:39,973 --> 00:57:41,181
- Or Weather Elizabethby.

1609
00:57:41,181 --> 00:57:42,735
- But I can't make you love me.

1610
00:57:45,392 --> 00:57:47,222
- Someday going to kill you.

1611
00:57:48,568 --> 00:57:51,640
- I should kill you.
- No, I should kill you.

1612
00:57:51,640 --> 00:57:52,986
- But the artist is vain.

1613
00:57:52,986 --> 00:57:54,678
- You mean Jeff Koons?

1614
00:57:54,678 --> 00:57:57,232
- He can't destroy the
 beauty he's created.

1615
00:57:59,268 --> 00:58:01,029
- Oh, I'm standing on you.

1616
00:58:01,029 --> 00:58:02,306
I'm sorry.

1617
00:58:02,306 --> 00:58:04,411
- Well, he is kind of cute.

1618
00:58:04,411 --> 00:58:08,795
♪ I don't know how to love him

1619
00:58:08,795 --> 00:58:09,796
- Hiya, doc.

1620
00:58:09,796 --> 00:58:11,591
- Look, my mouse melted.

1621
00:58:11,591 --> 00:58:12,454
- Oh, hello.

1622
00:58:12,454 --> 00:58:13,282
Come in.

1623
00:58:13,282 --> 00:58:14,491
- Look, I'm a scientist.

1624
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:16,803
- Lombardi tells me
he's coming here today.

1625
00:58:16,803 --> 00:58:18,356
- He's agreed to
conduct a demonstration

1626
00:58:18,356 --> 00:58:20,324
under clinical conditions.

1627
00:58:20,324 --> 00:58:21,498
- Mind if I sit in?

1628
00:58:22,740 --> 00:58:23,948
- No.

1629
00:58:23,948 --> 00:58:25,571
- I'd like to set-up
 a tape recorder.

1630
00:58:25,571 --> 00:58:27,952
- Nope, doing science.
 - Understand me, doc.

1631
00:58:27,952 --> 00:58:30,230
The man is a killer
 and I can't touch him.

1632
00:58:30,230 --> 00:58:31,508
♪ Can't touch this

1633
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:33,751
- Statement like that
 calls for some proof.

1634
00:58:33,751 --> 00:58:35,304
- I've got none.

1635
00:58:35,304 --> 00:58:37,272
All I know is he hates the
 world and everybody in it.

1636
00:58:37,272 --> 00:58:39,516
- With no food, gerbils died.

1637
00:58:40,827 --> 00:58:42,726
- Man kills for love, or...

1638
00:58:42,726 --> 00:58:45,591
- That other thing.
 - Hate, or profit.

1639
00:58:46,868 --> 00:58:48,283
Where do these killings fit in?

1640
00:58:48,283 --> 00:58:50,561
- All three, and don't
forget the profit angle.

1641
00:58:50,561 --> 00:58:52,770
Lombardi has become
quite a national figure.

1642
00:58:55,393 --> 00:58:58,155
I don't know if he's responsible
for those murders or not.

1643
00:58:58,155 --> 00:58:59,777
But I do know he's a
 very dangerous man.

1644
00:58:59,777 --> 00:59:01,745
- And he makes a
great breakfast.

1645
00:59:03,022 --> 00:59:04,610
- Dave Berg, scientist.

1646
00:59:06,335 --> 00:59:07,544
- Wah, haven't you left yet?

1647
00:59:07,544 --> 00:59:08,683
- You've lumped
 them all together.

1648
00:59:08,683 --> 00:59:11,617
Hypnotism, spiritualism,
age regression.

1649
00:59:11,617 --> 00:59:14,205
Reincarnation and
 soul transmigration.

1650
00:59:14,205 --> 00:59:16,207
♪ Soul

1651
00:59:16,207 --> 00:59:17,623
♪ Transmigration

1652
00:59:17,623 --> 00:59:19,556
We all have a secret
 willingness to believe

1653
00:59:19,556 --> 00:59:21,247
in some of the
 things he's offering.

1654
00:59:21,247 --> 00:59:22,697
- Green Stamps.

1655
00:59:22,697 --> 00:59:24,768
- The passing of the soul
 into another body after death.

1656
00:59:24,768 --> 00:59:26,079
That life is eternal.

1657
00:59:26,079 --> 00:59:27,840
That we can communicate
with the dead.

1658
00:59:27,840 --> 00:59:28,979
- Snow blowers that talk?

1659
00:59:28,979 --> 00:59:31,498
- Lombardi fancies
himself the miracle man

1660
00:59:31,498 --> 00:59:33,673
who's been granted the power
 to prove these things right.

1661
00:59:33,673 --> 00:59:36,607
- He's an egomaniac playing god.

1662
00:59:36,607 --> 00:59:39,472
He claims that the life
process is continuous,

1663
00:59:39,472 --> 00:59:41,785
that he can take it back
to a former existence

1664
00:59:41,785 --> 00:59:43,856
and not only communicate
with it, but cause it...

1665
00:59:43,856 --> 00:59:45,720
- Line?
 - To materialize.

1666
00:59:45,720 --> 00:59:47,929
To become a physical thing.
 - Can you stand it?

1667
00:59:47,929 --> 00:59:49,793
- According to Lombardi,
the She Creature

1668
00:59:49,793 --> 00:59:52,589
was the primitive life body
 of somebody living today.

1669
00:59:52,589 --> 00:59:54,521
- It was the strawberries.

1670
00:59:54,521 --> 00:59:56,454
- What do you make of that?

1671
00:59:56,454 --> 00:59:58,940
- We're still searching
for the answer.

1672
00:59:58,940 --> 01:00:00,044
- We found the answer.

1673
01:00:00,044 --> 01:00:01,598
The answer is her dress.

1674
01:00:01,598 --> 01:00:03,600
- Some of the details
 she's given previously

1675
01:00:03,600 --> 01:00:06,292
have been proven
 remarkably accurate.

1676
01:00:06,292 --> 01:00:07,949
That was the medallion
 that was given

1677
01:00:07,949 --> 01:00:09,813
to her husband by King Charles.

1678
01:00:09,813 --> 01:00:10,641
- What?

1679
01:00:10,641 --> 01:00:11,504
Am I in this scene?

1680
01:00:11,504 --> 01:00:12,678
What?

1681
01:00:12,678 --> 01:00:14,058
- It was found in a
grave near Ceries Brook.

1682
01:00:14,058 --> 01:00:16,474
The headstone read,
 "Elizabeth Wetherby Blystone,

1683
01:00:16,474 --> 01:00:19,167
1600 to 1651."

1684
01:00:19,167 --> 01:00:20,996
Then it was planted there.

1685
01:00:20,996 --> 01:00:22,619
- Oh, this is preposterous.

1686
01:00:22,619 --> 01:00:23,827
- For the love of Pete.

1687
01:00:23,827 --> 01:00:26,277
- Do you hold with this
nonsense, Erickson?

1688
01:00:26,277 --> 01:00:27,451
- My mind is open.

1689
01:00:27,451 --> 01:00:28,348
- As is my fly.

1690
01:00:28,348 --> 01:00:29,729
Thank you!

1691
01:00:29,729 --> 01:00:31,524
- Go on with your
 experiment, Mr. Lombardi.

1692
01:00:31,524 --> 01:00:32,629
- Hi.

1693
01:00:32,629 --> 01:00:33,906
- Dr. Lombardi.

1694
01:00:33,906 --> 01:00:34,734
- Of course.

1695
01:00:34,734 --> 01:00:35,908
- Mr. Lombardi.

1696
01:00:35,908 --> 01:00:37,495
- You know, it's quite
 simple, gentlemen,

1697
01:00:37,495 --> 01:00:39,601
to disbelieve anything that
 shatters your smug concepts.

1698
01:00:39,601 --> 01:00:41,085
- Yeah, stick it to the man!

1699
01:00:41,085 --> 01:00:43,398
- I'm taking this girl
 back to a time in her life

1700
01:00:43,398 --> 01:00:46,470
over 300 years ago.
 - To caveman times.

1701
01:00:46,470 --> 01:00:48,334
- Perhaps I can take her
back farther than that.

1702
01:00:48,334 --> 01:00:51,164
- Hey, Bunsen Honeydew.
 - To the time of the Pharaohs.

1703
01:00:52,476 --> 01:00:55,099
Even to the beginning
 of creation itself.

1704
01:00:55,099 --> 01:00:56,583
- Don't act, don't act.

1705
01:00:56,583 --> 01:00:59,000
- One soul, traveling
 the entire distance.

1706
01:01:00,208 --> 01:01:01,658
- Utter nonsense.
 - Thank you.

1707
01:01:01,658 --> 01:01:04,315
- I can materialize her
in any one of her lives.

1708
01:01:04,315 --> 01:01:06,317
- Let's just get her
 going in this one.

1709
01:01:06,317 --> 01:01:08,078
- I can transport her
 from what she is...

1710
01:01:08,078 --> 01:01:09,527
- To what she is.

1711
01:01:09,527 --> 01:01:12,461
- To what she was.
 - Oh, bull cookies.

1712
01:01:12,461 --> 01:01:15,637
- Really, lieutenant, are
 we supposed to watch this?

1713
01:01:15,637 --> 01:01:17,915
This is penny arcade drama.

1714
01:01:17,915 --> 01:01:19,192
- Doctor, have I ever
been alone in this room?

1715
01:01:19,192 --> 01:01:20,918
- Not while I was here.

1716
01:01:20,918 --> 01:01:23,507
[upbeat music]

1717
01:01:27,097 --> 01:01:28,512
- Hi honey, you there?

1718
01:01:29,409 --> 01:01:31,066
- I'm talking to you, Elizabeth.

1719
01:01:31,066 --> 01:01:32,171
- But I'm not touching you.

1720
01:01:32,171 --> 01:01:33,379
Does this bug you?

1721
01:01:33,379 --> 01:01:34,207
- You're going
 into a deep sleep.

1722
01:01:34,207 --> 01:01:35,968
- Huh, big surprise.

1723
01:01:35,968 --> 01:01:37,417
- Very deep.

1724
01:01:37,417 --> 01:01:39,212
- Imagine you don't
 have a mustache.

1725
01:01:41,490 --> 01:01:43,458
He's so expressive.

1726
01:01:43,458 --> 01:01:45,978
- She's not responding.
- We need jumper cables.

1727
01:01:45,978 --> 01:01:48,808
- Someone in this room is
 fighting me for her will.

1728
01:01:48,808 --> 01:01:51,431
- And you'll stay after
until I find out who.

1729
01:01:51,431 --> 01:01:52,570
- Is it you, doctor?

1730
01:01:54,883 --> 01:01:56,609
- Yes, I'm sorry.

1731
01:01:56,609 --> 01:01:58,162
- I thought it was
 someone else's will.

1732
01:01:58,162 --> 01:01:59,716
I'm sorry.

1733
01:01:59,716 --> 01:02:02,719
- A deep sleep, Elizabeth.
 - Chicago style.

1734
01:02:02,719 --> 01:02:06,515
- Very deep.
 - Very Chicago style.

1735
01:02:06,515 --> 01:02:07,827
- That's better.

1736
01:02:09,035 --> 01:02:12,142
You are now suspended
 in time and space.

1737
01:02:12,142 --> 01:02:14,144
- A dimension not of sight
 and sound but of mind.

1738
01:02:14,144 --> 01:02:15,870
- Now I'm going to
 give you a substance.

1739
01:02:15,870 --> 01:02:17,837
- In my Zappa boots.

1740
01:02:17,837 --> 01:02:19,459
- Not form, but substance.

1741
01:02:20,391 --> 01:02:21,979
- You are in a thick sauce.

1742
01:02:21,979 --> 01:02:24,671
- You will take back the
 soul that once was yours.

1743
01:02:24,671 --> 01:02:26,156
- And take back all
 my empty beer bottles.

1744
01:02:26,156 --> 01:02:28,572
- Andrea will give it to you.

1745
01:02:29,607 --> 01:02:31,333
- Yes, I snuck a peek at you.

1746
01:02:31,333 --> 01:02:32,162
I'm sorry.

1747
01:02:33,335 --> 01:02:34,405
- Now, put...

1748
01:02:35,821 --> 01:02:38,202
You can express
 yourself in movement.

1749
01:02:38,202 --> 01:02:39,894
- No, not interpretive
 dance, no.

1750
01:02:44,277 --> 01:02:46,590
- He boldly plays a
 guy who stands there.

1751
01:02:48,557 --> 01:02:51,319
- It's just menthol
 action, folks, don't worry.

1752
01:02:53,735 --> 01:02:56,807
- Who let one?

1753
01:02:56,807 --> 01:02:57,635
Ugh.

1754
01:02:58,809 --> 01:03:00,328
- Oh dear, oh cripes.

1755
01:03:00,328 --> 01:03:03,158
- Would you take Professor
Anderson's glasses off, please?

1756
01:03:08,094 --> 01:03:09,786
- Well, this is
 highly irregular.

1757
01:03:09,786 --> 01:03:11,926
Whoa, wow, wow, whoa.

1758
01:03:11,926 --> 01:03:14,204
- Put them back on.

1759
01:03:14,204 --> 01:03:15,757
- Or, just reverse the film.

1760
01:03:18,967 --> 01:03:21,211
- That is enough, Elizabeth.

1761
01:03:21,211 --> 01:03:23,869
I think we've convinced them.
 - Ah yeah, they're convinced.

1762
01:03:23,869 --> 01:03:27,562
- Would you return Andrea's
 soul to her, please?

1763
01:03:27,562 --> 01:03:28,390
Thank you.

1764
01:03:29,529 --> 01:03:31,635
- She's got visible
 something line.

1765
01:03:35,501 --> 01:03:37,537
- Those who believe
 can actually see

1766
01:03:37,537 --> 01:03:40,057
the process of transmigration.

1767
01:03:40,057 --> 01:03:41,265
- I saw nothing.

1768
01:03:41,265 --> 01:03:42,232
- Nor I.

1769
01:03:43,578 --> 01:03:44,648
- Trickery.
- Dickery dock.

1770
01:03:44,648 --> 01:03:47,478
- Very clever, Dr. Lombardi.

1771
01:03:47,478 --> 01:03:49,411
But absolutely meaningless.

1772
01:03:49,411 --> 01:03:51,068
- Come on, I worked
 really hard on that.

1773
01:03:51,068 --> 01:03:53,208
- You can't see because
you don't wish to see.

1774
01:03:53,208 --> 01:03:54,416
- Just wait out
 the scene, Lance.

1775
