01:13:06,796 --> 01:13:08,453
- He will never have you.

2029
01:13:08,453 --> 01:13:10,109
- Look into my
 upsetting mustache.

2030
01:13:10,109 --> 01:13:12,940
- I'll kill him.
- You'd do that for me?

2031
01:13:14,182 --> 01:13:15,770
I'm sorry, what were you saying?

2032
01:13:17,462 --> 01:13:19,567
- Look deep into my eyebags.

2033
01:13:20,741 --> 01:13:23,606
- You'll kill him.
 - Come on, come on.

2034
01:13:23,606 --> 01:13:24,434
You want some?

2035
01:13:24,434 --> 01:13:25,401
What you got, huh?

2036
01:13:25,401 --> 01:13:26,229
Huh?

2037
01:13:26,229 --> 01:13:27,437
I'm taking you down.

2038
01:13:27,437 --> 01:13:29,197
- This time you
 will do as I say.

2039
01:13:29,197 --> 01:13:32,131
- Viewers are invited to
 finish the scene themselves.

2040
01:13:32,131 --> 01:13:34,720
- I haven't seen you and
 Dorothy together much lately.

2041
01:13:34,720 --> 01:13:35,549
What's the matter?

2042
01:13:35,549 --> 01:13:36,412
Lovers' quarrel?

2043
01:13:36,412 --> 01:13:37,240
- You haven't heard.

2044
01:13:37,240 --> 01:13:38,690
I'm not in this movie.

2045
01:13:38,690 --> 01:13:41,693
- Well, here's something that
 will help you patch it up.

2046
01:13:41,693 --> 01:13:43,073
- Arnold Stang's autograph.

2047
01:13:43,073 --> 01:13:44,005
Should fetch a pretty penny.

2048
01:13:44,005 --> 01:13:45,628
- $250,000.

2049
01:13:45,628 --> 01:13:46,663
Dorothy's.

2050
01:13:46,663 --> 01:13:47,561
- And yours.

2051
01:13:47,561 --> 01:13:49,079
You helped to set it up.

2052
01:13:49,079 --> 01:13:50,667
There's more coming in.

2053
01:13:50,667 --> 01:13:51,875
Go over and show it to her.

2054
01:13:51,875 --> 01:13:53,981
She doesn't know
 anything about it.

2055
01:13:53,981 --> 01:13:56,639
This'll help you to forget
 Carlo's little girl, eh?

2056
01:13:56,639 --> 01:13:58,157
Hmm.

2057
01:13:58,157 --> 01:14:00,505
- I don't think I could forget
 where the money came from.

2058
01:14:00,505 --> 01:14:02,438
I told you I was a
fool about such things.

2059
01:14:02,438 --> 01:14:04,543
I'm sure I'll never have
 another offer like that again,

2060
01:14:04,543 --> 01:14:05,717
but thanks for giving
 me the first offer.

2061
01:14:05,717 --> 01:14:06,925
- Hey, he's moving,
 look at that.

2062
01:14:06,925 --> 01:14:09,065
The scene was actually blocked.

2063
01:14:10,446 --> 01:14:11,308
- Hi, Ted.

2064
01:14:11,308 --> 01:14:12,240
- Hi, little fella.

2065
01:14:12,240 --> 01:14:13,449
- Who are you looking for?

2066
01:14:13,449 --> 01:14:15,520
Andrea Elizabeth or
 Elizabeth Andrea?

2067
01:14:15,520 --> 01:14:17,867
I saw both of her down
 near the ocean a while ago.

2068
01:14:17,867 --> 01:14:18,868
- Thanks.

2069
01:14:18,868 --> 01:14:19,800
- Ted.

2070
01:14:19,800 --> 01:14:22,734
What's she got that I haven't?

2071
01:14:22,734 --> 01:14:24,494
- Money, breeding,
 social position?

2072
01:14:24,494 --> 01:14:25,357
- Don't answer.

2073
01:14:25,357 --> 01:14:26,531
It's a trap.

2074
01:14:26,531 --> 01:14:28,533
- Some people have too
 much of everything.

2075
01:14:28,533 --> 01:14:30,327
- You don't have
 enough of anything.

2076
01:14:30,327 --> 01:14:31,605
- Guess I had that coming.

2077
01:14:32,468 --> 01:14:33,710
She's a nice girl, Ted.

2078
01:14:36,402 --> 01:14:38,094
- Well, it was nice meeting you.

2079
01:14:38,094 --> 01:14:40,199
- Thanks for the Bob
 Dole handshake, jerk.

2080
01:14:42,650 --> 01:14:44,894
- Ah, here comes Marty
 Markham to the rescue.

2081
01:14:46,654 --> 01:14:47,793
- Hi, beautiful.

2082
01:14:47,793 --> 01:14:48,622
- Bob.

2083
01:14:48,622 --> 01:14:49,485
- Hi, fallback.

2084
01:14:49,485 --> 01:14:50,658
- What are you drinking?

2085
01:14:50,658 --> 01:14:54,006
That's a scotch,
 bourbon, gin cocktail.

2086
01:14:54,006 --> 01:14:55,594
- No vodka?

2087
01:14:55,594 --> 01:14:57,251
You must be tapering off.

2088
01:14:57,251 --> 01:14:58,528
Let me know when you
 get down to the scotch

2089
01:14:58,528 --> 01:14:59,736
and bourbon cocktails.

2090
01:14:59,736 --> 01:15:01,773
- It's neat that she's
interested in his hobby.

2091
01:15:03,775 --> 01:15:05,604
- There goes the gin.

2092
01:15:05,604 --> 01:15:07,848
Now I'm down to a bourbon
 and scotch cocktail.

2093
01:15:07,848 --> 01:15:10,506
- And the hydrangea bushes
 die a horrible death.

2094
01:15:12,369 --> 01:15:13,509
- Some squirrels down
there are going to have

2095
01:15:13,509 --> 01:15:14,648
a kick-ass party.

2096
01:15:16,995 --> 01:15:18,652
- This means you're
 cured of alcoholism

2097
01:15:18,652 --> 01:15:22,000
and you'll never have any
 bouts of booze drinking again.

2098
01:15:22,000 --> 01:15:25,106
- Sessions presents Summer Gold.

2099
01:15:25,106 --> 01:15:27,108
- Gee, I'm supposed to
 do a kids' birthday party

2100
01:15:27,108 --> 01:15:28,385
around here somewhere.

2101
01:15:29,525 --> 01:15:30,664
- You taught me
 how to fight him.

2102
01:15:30,664 --> 01:15:32,217
His power is gone.
 - Really?

2103
01:15:32,217 --> 01:15:34,219
When did I do that?

2104
01:15:34,219 --> 01:15:35,565
- We'd better be getting
back to the house.

2105
01:15:35,565 --> 01:15:37,636
He'll be looking for you.

2106
01:15:37,636 --> 01:15:39,362
- I don't want to go
through with it tonight.

2107
01:15:39,362 --> 01:15:41,019
- Kissing me is
 hard, I know, but...

2108
01:15:41,019 --> 01:15:42,365
- You've got to.

2109
01:15:42,365 --> 01:15:44,367
Resist him publicly and
he'll leave you alone.

2110
01:15:44,367 --> 01:15:45,644
- Or bury a toad at midnight.

2111
01:15:45,644 --> 01:15:46,507
I don't know.

2112
01:15:46,507 --> 01:15:47,784
- What if I don't?

2113
01:15:47,784 --> 01:15:49,890
- I'll retain my
 football-shaped head.

2114
01:15:50,856 --> 01:15:52,375
- I'll fight him for you.

2115
01:15:52,375 --> 01:15:53,169
- No, wait, I won't.

2116
01:15:53,169 --> 01:15:54,101
Forget it.

2117
01:15:54,101 --> 01:15:55,585
- I think I'll win.

2118
01:15:55,585 --> 01:15:56,931
- By the way, do you know
 why we love each other?

2119
01:15:56,931 --> 01:15:58,139
I don't.

2120
01:15:58,139 --> 01:16:00,763
- Just stay here a
 little longer with me.

2121
01:16:00,763 --> 01:16:03,455
- Okay, how's this?

2122
01:16:03,455 --> 01:16:04,974
- Jeez, I lost my doves too.

2123
01:16:04,974 --> 01:16:06,147
What next?

2124
01:16:08,253 --> 01:16:10,048
Did you bring the Frisbee?

2125
01:16:14,949 --> 01:16:16,779
- Hey, can you pull
 my stitches out, bud?

2126
01:16:16,779 --> 01:16:18,884
[dog barking]

2127
01:16:18,884 --> 01:16:20,161
- You can kill him.

2128
01:16:20,161 --> 01:16:21,680
- What?
- I command you.

2129
01:16:21,680 --> 01:16:23,268
- Huh?

2130
01:16:23,268 --> 01:16:25,097
- Yes, King, I will kill him.

2131
01:16:27,306 --> 01:16:28,791
- But you didn't
 even throw a stick.

2132
01:16:28,791 --> 01:16:31,552
[dramatic music]

2133
01:16:32,795 --> 01:16:33,623
- Manics!

2134
01:16:33,623 --> 01:16:36,143
[dog barking]

2135
01:16:37,558 --> 01:16:38,421
- Well, good luck.

2136
01:16:39,422 --> 01:16:40,423
- It's not me growling.

2137
01:16:40,423 --> 01:16:41,389
They dubbed it in.

2138
01:16:42,943 --> 01:16:44,254
- Ah, I'm a pirate.

2139
01:16:44,254 --> 01:16:45,221
Arr.
 - Get away.

2140
01:16:45,221 --> 01:16:46,740
He's going crazy.

2141
01:16:46,740 --> 01:16:48,569
- His prices are way too low.

2142
01:16:50,019 --> 01:16:52,228
- Just had Novocaine.
 - Get away.

2143
01:16:52,228 --> 01:16:53,470
[dog growling]

2144
01:16:53,470 --> 01:16:54,368
- Sorry I lashed out
 at you with the thing.

2145
01:16:54,368 --> 01:16:57,267
[dog whimpers]

2146
01:16:57,267 --> 01:16:59,131
- I don't wanna be in movies.

2147
01:16:59,131 --> 01:17:01,617
I just wanna eat bacon
 strips and chase cars.

2148
01:17:03,653 --> 01:17:05,759
- That had no effect on me.

2149
01:17:05,759 --> 01:17:07,726
- That voice didn't
 come from me.

2150
01:17:07,726 --> 01:17:08,589
- Yes it did.

2151
01:17:10,556 --> 01:17:13,145
- Let's get away from here.
 - Let's stand over there.

2152
01:17:13,145 --> 01:17:13,974
Better.

2153
01:17:16,114 --> 01:17:18,944
- We're ready to start, if
 you'll just, if you could sit.

2154
01:17:20,118 --> 01:17:21,671
- Hey, can I see you a minute?

2155
01:17:21,671 --> 01:17:23,500
- I think I killed
 that Swedish guy.

2156
01:17:23,500 --> 01:17:24,916
- I've formed a
 few theories by now

2157
01:17:24,916 --> 01:17:26,124
and I want to try
 them out on you.

2158
01:17:26,124 --> 01:17:27,643
- Santa is the killer.
 - I'm listening.

2159
01:17:27,643 --> 01:17:28,954
- Every time this
 thing has struck,

2160
01:17:28,954 --> 01:17:30,646
it's been after one of
 these demonstrations.

2161
01:17:30,646 --> 01:17:32,371
- See?
 - That's been the pattern.

2162
01:17:32,371 --> 01:17:33,890
I checked it.

2163
01:17:33,890 --> 01:17:36,272
- You think he has some way of
 signaling to his accomplices?

2164
01:17:36,272 --> 01:17:37,204
- I can hear you.

2165
01:17:37,204 --> 01:17:38,550
- If you can call them that.

2166
01:17:38,550 --> 01:17:40,863
Another thing I've discovered.
 - I'm part woman.

2167
01:17:40,863 --> 01:17:43,210
- Every time we find
 the footprints coming
 out of the ocean,

2168
01:17:43,210 --> 01:17:46,765
they go back, exactly
 the same spot.

2169
01:17:46,765 --> 01:17:48,215
- You're going on
 the assumption that

2170
01:17:48,215 --> 01:17:49,975
Lombardi's creature
 is the real thing.

2171
01:17:49,975 --> 01:17:52,012
- It's the only
 thing I can go on.

2172
01:17:52,012 --> 01:17:54,083
Otherwise it's the
 psychopathic ward for me.

2173
01:17:54,083 --> 01:17:55,325
- Hey, Chet Baker,
 security guard.

2174
01:17:55,325 --> 01:17:56,741
- I'm not sure,
 what do you think?

2175
01:17:56,741 --> 01:17:59,640
- As a scientist I'm
 hysterical with laughter.

2176
01:17:59,640 --> 01:18:02,988
As a man out for a social
 evening, I'm not so sure.

2177
01:18:02,988 --> 01:18:04,852
In fact, very unsure.

2178
01:18:04,852 --> 01:18:06,302
- All right, folks.

2179
01:18:06,302 --> 01:18:07,683
Showtime.

2180
01:18:07,683 --> 01:18:08,925
House lights out, please.

2181
01:18:10,686 --> 01:18:12,826
- Hey, send Olaf
 out here, will you?

2182
01:18:13,689 --> 01:18:14,551
- Sure.

2183
01:18:16,726 --> 01:18:18,694
- Hey, Fanny and
 Alexander, listen up.

2184
01:18:19,798 --> 01:18:21,248
- Lieutenant James
 wants to speak to you.

2185
01:18:21,248 --> 01:18:22,352
- Oh.

2186
01:18:22,352 --> 01:18:23,457
- Out on the terrace.
 - Yes, sir.

2187
01:18:23,457 --> 01:18:24,803
- I'm making Hellraiser.

2188
01:18:25,839 --> 01:18:27,392
- Am I under arrest, I hope?

2189
01:18:27,392 --> 01:18:30,326
I sure would like to get
 away from this spook shop.

2190
01:18:30,326 --> 01:18:32,293
- Hey, have you got
 a tape recorder?

2191
01:18:32,293 --> 01:18:33,709
- In Mr. Chappel's study.

2192
01:18:33,709 --> 01:18:35,469
- Can you take me there
without going through

2193
01:18:35,469 --> 01:18:36,263
the living room?

2194
01:18:36,263 --> 01:18:37,091
- Oh, yeah, sure.

2195
01:18:37,091 --> 01:18:38,575
Come right this way.

2196
01:18:38,575 --> 01:18:40,474
- That was my favorite
 scene in the whole movie.

2197
01:18:42,752 --> 01:18:43,719
- Right here, sir.

2198
01:18:44,789 --> 01:18:46,031
- Thank you.

2199
01:18:46,031 --> 01:18:46,963
- Two giants of
 the film industry

2200
01:18:46,963 --> 01:18:48,413
finally have a scene together.

2201
01:18:50,829 --> 01:18:52,762
- Ladies and gentlemen, "Stomp."

2202
01:18:55,385 --> 01:18:56,835
- I will touch you gently.

2203
01:18:58,043 --> 01:18:59,562
And you will fall
 into a deep sleep.

2204
01:18:59,562 --> 01:19:01,737
- You have a little
chicken gravy up there.

2205
01:19:03,014 --> 01:19:04,740
- Your eyes are getting heavy.

2206
01:19:04,740 --> 01:19:06,362
- Always criticize my weight.

2207
01:19:06,362 --> 01:19:08,122
- They're starting to close now.

2208
01:19:09,883 --> 01:19:10,746
- Sorry.

2209
01:19:10,746 --> 01:19:12,092
You're on your own.

2210
01:19:12,092 --> 01:19:13,576
- Ooh, who jiffed in here?

2211
01:19:13,576 --> 01:19:14,404
Oof.

2212
01:19:15,854 --> 01:19:17,580
- So he's backfired.

2213
01:19:17,580 --> 01:19:19,340
- He's right.
 - I'm dying up here.

2214
01:19:20,514 --> 01:19:22,309
- I will count to four.

2215
01:19:22,309 --> 01:19:24,898
And you will fall into
 a deep, deep sleep.

2216
01:19:26,451 --> 01:19:27,279
One.

2217
01:19:28,280 --> 01:19:29,109
Two.

2218
01:19:29,109 --> 01:19:30,213
- 39.

2219
01:19:30,213 --> 01:19:31,042
- Three.

2220
01:19:32,284 --> 01:19:33,803
Four.

2221
01:19:33,803 --> 01:19:36,116
- Ha-ha-ha, my will is in my
 purse and you can't have it.

2222
01:19:37,220 --> 01:19:38,187
- She's hypnotized.

2223
01:19:38,187 --> 01:19:39,636
Thank you!

2224
01:19:39,636 --> 01:19:40,810
- Ladies and gentlemen, my
subject is not herself tonight.

2225
01:19:40,810 --> 01:19:42,294
She's is too tense.

2226
01:19:42,294 --> 01:19:44,158
- She's a tepee and a wigwam.

2227
01:19:44,158 --> 01:19:44,987
- Woo!

2228
01:19:46,298 --> 01:19:47,783
- Come on, sleep.

2229
01:19:47,783 --> 01:19:49,163
- Will you take your place
 on the couch, please?

2230
01:19:49,163 --> 01:19:51,269
- No, you sleep on
 the couch tonight.

2231
01:19:54,168 --> 01:19:56,308
They should do a jump
 ball for her soul.

2232
01:19:57,482 --> 01:19:59,208
- What exactly is
 their act again?

2233
01:20:01,003 --> 01:20:02,659
- Dumb, stupid audience.

2234
01:20:02,659 --> 01:20:05,386
Jeez.

2235
01:20:05,386 --> 01:20:06,318
Ew.

2236
01:20:06,318 --> 01:20:08,148
- You have eyes only for mine.

2237
01:20:09,563 --> 01:20:11,979
You have ears only for my voice.

2238
01:20:11,979 --> 01:20:14,430
- Nose only for my scent.

2239
01:20:14,430 --> 01:20:16,950
- Now you're going
 into a deep sleep.

2240
01:20:16,950 --> 01:20:18,261
Your eyes are heavy.

2241
01:20:19,642 --> 01:20:22,024
Close your eyes and
 go into a deep sleep.

2242
01:20:22,024 --> 01:20:24,474
- Like when you're on a
date with Lance Fuller.

2243
01:20:24,474 --> 01:20:25,303
- Deeper.

2244
01:20:26,822 --> 01:20:27,719
- Deeper.

2245
01:20:27,719 --> 01:20:28,547
- Come on.

2246
01:20:28,547 --> 01:20:29,376
I call.

2247
01:20:31,309 --> 01:20:33,035
- Maybe if we did the wave.

2248
01:20:33,898 --> 01:20:35,382
- She's dead.

2249
01:20:35,382 --> 01:20:36,866
[Mike and Crow laugh]

2250
01:20:36,866 --> 01:20:40,042
- Said before you were giving
 her substance, but not form.

2251
01:20:40,042 --> 01:20:41,319
- What did you mean by that?

2252
01:20:41,319 --> 01:20:42,803
- I don't like this
 new Prince album.

2253
01:20:42,803 --> 01:20:45,426
- [Carlo] I could have brought
 her to you in the flesh.

2254
01:20:45,426 --> 01:20:47,912
Just as she was 300 years ago.

2255
01:20:47,912 --> 01:20:50,190
- That's all the evidence
 I need, whatever it was.

2256
01:20:50,190 --> 01:20:52,261
- I'm talking toyou, Elizabeth.

2257
01:20:52,261 --> 01:20:53,883
- Elizabeth Ann She Creature.

2258
01:20:53,883 --> 01:20:55,264
- Where were you born?

2259
01:20:55,264 --> 01:20:56,782
- He's doing all his old stuff.

2260
01:20:58,198 --> 01:21:01,857
- Man, I am taking the
 pipe so bad right now.

2261
01:21:01,857 --> 01:21:04,721
- My subject is disturbed
 tonight, ladies and gentlemen.

2262
01:21:04,721 --> 01:21:06,896
Her world is disturbed.

2263
01:21:06,896 --> 01:21:09,381
I feel a menace to the
 people in this house.

2264
01:21:09,381 --> 01:21:11,763
I urge you all to
 leave here at once.

2265
01:21:11,763 --> 01:21:12,833
- Do as he says, everybody.

2266
01:21:12,833 --> 01:21:14,007
Let's clear out of here.

2267
01:21:14,007 --> 01:21:15,215
- But be sure to
 tip your waitresses

2268
01:21:15,215 --> 01:21:16,492
and drive carefully
 on the way home.

2269
01:21:16,492 --> 01:21:17,320
Goodnight!

2270
01:21:18,528 --> 01:21:19,529
- No one's forced
 me out of my home.

2271
01:21:19,529 --> 01:21:21,359
- Is anybody listening to me?

2272
01:21:23,361 --> 01:21:25,639
- So you want to end
this movie or something?

2273
01:21:26,882 --> 01:21:28,884
- Get her out of it.
 - Perhaps you can.

2274
01:21:29,885 --> 01:21:31,472
- Whoa!

2275
01:21:31,472 --> 01:21:33,405
- You kill me and you kill her.

2276
01:21:33,405 --> 01:21:35,614
- You kill her, you
 kill Anson Williams.

2277
01:21:35,614 --> 01:21:38,134
[upbeat music]

2278
01:21:41,793 --> 01:21:42,828
[tense music]

2279
01:21:42,828 --> 01:21:44,037
- This is probably best.

2280
01:21:44,037 --> 01:21:45,279
He couldn't outrun
 it or anything.

2281
01:21:45,279 --> 01:21:47,316
[gunshots banging]

